185-- The factory function is called once, when the runtime initializes the agent.
186-- The returned value is duck-type checked (`exec`, `getCwd`, and an `fs` object). A wrong value throws `Error('[flue] BashFactory must return a Bash-like object.')`.
187-- The sandbox's `cwd` is the instance's `getCwd()` (just-bash defaults to `/home/user` when constructed without `cwd` or `files`).
188-- just-bash has no native timeout option, so the wrapper translates `exec`'s `timeoutMs` into an `AbortSignal` and merges it with the caller's signal. Pre- and post-call abort checks apply as in `sandboxFromDriver`.
189-- The `writeFile` parent-creation guarantee is applied over the instance's `fs`.
