200:## Custom hooks
201:Because hooks are plain function calls, you can extract related declarations into named, reusable pieces the same way React does: with **custom hooks**. A custom hook is a function that you define yourself, always prefixed with `use`. It may take arguments and return values to its caller, just like any other function:
202-```ts title="src/agents/support-assistant.ts"
203-import { useModel, useTool } from '@flue/runtime';
204-import { escalateCase } from '../shared/support-tools.ts';
205-function useEscalation() {
206-  useTool(escalateCase);
207-  return 'Escalate to a specialist only after you have confirmed the account and issue.';
208-}
209-function SupportAssistant() {
210-  useModel('anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5');
211-  const escalationInstructions = useEscalation();
212-  return `Answer customer support questions accurately. ${escalationInstructions}`;
213-}
214-```
215:Custom hooks are how larger agents stay readable, and how capabilities get shared across agents — a `useGitHub()` hook that bundles the right tools, skills, and instructions can be written once and dropped into every agent that works with GitHub.
