122-## What registration does not change
123:- **Pi's catalog itself.** A registration shadows one provider ID at resolution time; it never adds, removes, or edits catalog entries.
124:- **Anything durable.** Registrations live in process memory for the current module scope. They are not persisted, not shared across processes or isolates, and rebuilt from module top-level code on every boot.
125-- **Earlier registrations of other provider IDs.** Each call affects exactly one provider ID.

