211:## `SandboxToolFactory`
212-```ts
213-type SandboxToolFactory = (sandbox: Sandbox, options: SandboxToolFactoryOptions) => AgentTool<any>[];
214-interface SandboxToolFactoryOptions {
215-  subagents: Record<string, SubagentDefinition>;
216-}
217-```
218-An optional `tools` function on a `SandboxFactory`. When present, its return value **replaces** the framework's default six-tool set (`read`, `write`, `edit`, `bash`, `grep`, `glob`) for agents on this sandbox. Compose the replacement from the [standard tool factories](#the-standard-tool-factories) plus the sandbox's own native tools rather than rebuilding from scratch — an exec-less sandbox, for example, lists the three file tools and its own executor tool.
219-- Must be synchronous and return a fresh array on every call. It is invoked each time the runtime assembles the model's tool list — at initialization and again at every turn boundary — not once.
220-- `sandbox` — the live sandbox, with the [packaged-skill overlay](#packaged-skill-overlays) layered onto `readFile`. This is not the identical object `harness.sandbox` exposes; tools that hold the sandbox in a closure read packaged-skill paths transparently.
221-- `options.subagents` — the agent's current subagent roster, keyed by name. Provided for adapters whose tools describe or constrain delegation.
222-The replacement covers only the framework's built-in group. Unaffected by it:
223-- The framework group — `task` (always present), `activate_skill` (when any skill is mounted), and `read_skill_resource` (when a mounted packaged skill carries supporting files) — is appended separately.
224-- Custom tools from `useTool(...)` / `defineTool(...)` and per-call result tools are added separately.
225-Tool names must be unique across all groups, and the names `task`, `activate_skill`, `read_skill_resource`, `finish`, and `give_up` are framework-reserved. A collision throws [`ToolNameConflictError`](/docs/reference/errors/#toolnameconflicterror) when the tool list is assembled.
226-The element type is `AgentTool` from `@earendil-works/pi-agent-core` (a dependency of `@flue/runtime`; the type is not re-exported). Structurally:
227-```ts
228-interface AgentTool<TParameters extends TSchema = TSchema, TDetails = any> {
229-  name: string;
230-  label: string;
231-  description: string;
232-  parameters: TParameters; // TypeBox schema
233-  execute(
234-    toolCallId: string,
235-    params: Static<TParameters>,
236-    signal?: AbortSignal,
237-    onUpdate?: (partial: AgentToolResult<TDetails>) => void,
238-  ): Promise<AgentToolResult<TDetails>>; // { content, details, terminate? }
239-}
