origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:102:{"id":"wt-391-forward-6gd.1","title":"SBX1.1: bind static remote-worker protocol + placement to landed SandboxProviderV1","description":"SBX1.1 — Delivers: Gate-C re-inventory; shared strict protocol schemas; static fleet config/bucket resolver; per-box short-lived capability auth including bounded SSE lifetime; V1 client/provider pair; stable errors; the named H5 `sandboxId <-> authorized workspaceId` tenant-binding invariant with authenticated create binding receipt; and the H3 seam replacing heuristic `withRuntimeEnvContributions()` plaintext merging with purpose-typed per-workspace secret references. Decision 27 model BYOK stays at the landed #820 host Pi request seam and is rejected by remote-worker/Sandbox exec; only non-model invocation-secret references may reach the worker stdin envelope. Extend #820 owner-only credential lifecycle with an explicit disabled/revoked tombstone that suppresses instance fallback, plus upstream-revocation receipt/state; clear/absence retains Decision 27 fallback semantics.\nBlocked by (gates, captured as prerequisites not bead edges so this is the ready/dispatchable head of the chain): Gates A-D and the tracker transaction; completed #808 Phase 1-3 swap/artifact proof; merged #820 16f.2 host-side per-request credential seam.\nProof/exit: Sandbox/Core/Agent focused build/typecheck/test/invariants; strict config, missing-workspace, per-box-token, capability-expiry, and SSE-expiry/invalidation negatives; pair lifecycle/idempotency/expiry/dispose/error tests; two-workspace x two-sandbox cross-product rejection on fs/events/exec/renew/delete before adapters (the tested tenant-binding invariant); authenticated-receipt/swapped-create-response rejection; Decision 27 rotation visible at the next host model request; owner-only emergency disable creates a durable tombstone, suppresses fallback immediately, best-effort aborts the active request, and requires upstream revocation receipt/state before resolved; clear/absence still uses the explicit Decision 27 fallback; retained Sandbox-exec no-model-key proof; purpose/model/cross-workspace reference negatives; non-model stdin-envelope proof; Agent value-import invariant. 6gd.1 does not pass without every H3 and H5 gate.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-20T09:06:10.596851043Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-22T04:32:56.993735808Z","closed_at":"2026-07-22T04:32:56.993569044Z","close_reason":"SBX1.1 merged as #855 (1a9d5b007)","source_repo":"sbx1-activation","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/sbx1-activation","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","808"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-6gd.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-6gd","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T09:06:10.596851043Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:107:{"id":"wt-391-forward-6gd.6","title":"SBX1.6: canary and flip the SaaS default to own-cloud remote-worker","description":"SBX1.6 — Delivers: Existing-workspace inventory; bounded metadata-preserving forward/reverse cutover utility or empty proof; staging/canary; static production fleet config; default config flip; Vercel preservation and rollback playbooks.\nBlocked by: SBX1.5 (in-chain bead edge); plus external gates captured as prerequisites: merged #807 807-T1.4 durability/recovery proof, merged #820 16f.3 host conformance, owner cutover approval.\nProof/exit: Exact-artifact SaaS journey; independent POSIX manifests or empty proof; qualified-worker health; #807 task interruption/replay proof under box loss; Decision 27 host-key/Sandbox-negative proof; config proof; reverse-copy rollback rehearsal; Vercel conformance.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-20T09:06:11.116604633Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-20T09:06:12.253677934Z","source_repo":"sbx1-activation","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/sbx1-activation","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","808"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-6gd.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-6gd","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T09:06:11.116604633Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-6gd.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-6gd.5","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T09:06:12.252600107Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:111:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","title":"#391/#805 Decision 28: application Agent fleet, Workspace orchestration, and Environment service","description":"## Context\nDecision 28 supersedes the former Decision 26 typed-product/Step-1A graph. This epic now coordinates #391/#805 delivery of one deployment-static AgentApplication fleet, ordinary Workspace-owned persisted defaults and sessions, independent Core/web and CLI consumers, Workspace orchestration, and one governed `boring-bash` Environment service over Agent/Workspace-neutral `boring-sandbox` providers.\n\n## Durable invariants\n- Signup hostname initializes only a new Workspace default; it never grants membership, filters a portfolio, routes an existing Workspace, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Web membership and CLI trusted-local policy are the only consumer access authorities.\n- Workspace owns fleet/default/session/governance/orchestration. Agent owns one service-shaped in-process application. Core and CLI are peers and never boot/route through each other.\n- All file/search/watch/exec surfaces use one authoritative Environment API/filesystem; no copy/sync architecture.\n- Governance compiles invocation-scoped views; model credentials and shell grants are separate capabilities; providers fail closed when physical requirements are unsupported.\n- Expand, migrate, conformance, owner-approved contraction, contracted release-candidate proof, owner publication approval, then exact publication.\n\n## Graph policy\nThe Decision-28 F-series children are the only dispatchable implementation graph. Former R1-R6/C1-C4/I1 descendants are deferred historical Decision-26 snapshots. Closed R0 and R4 descendants remain closed evidence and are not reimplemented. Every child stays in_progress until its implementation PR merges.\n\n## Authority\nDecision 28 in docs/DECISIONS.md; product gates in docs/issues/391/plan.md; normative contracts, dependency edges, proof/review/rollback and Human Intention gates in docs/issues/805/runtime-refactor/work/A1-agent-authoring/WORKSPACE-AGENT-FLEET-PLAN.md.","acceptance_criteria":"All Decision-28 children through F8b are closed by merged PR/proof; H2c and H8 contain explicit owner approvals; conditional H4a is either untriggered with clean audit evidence or resolved through an owner-approved graph amendment; closed R0/R4 evidence remains linked; no former Decision-26 child is dispatchable; Core/web and CLI independently pass the contracted packed cohort with canonical no-copy Environment, persisted-default/session, rollback, and Seneca proof.","status":"in_progress","priority":0,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:34.777793350Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:12:59.106609678Z","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","agent-fleet","decision-28","environment-service"]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:112:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1","title":"#805 foundation: WorkspaceRuntime, typed bindings, declarative A1, regular dev","description":"## Context\nReplacement for wt-391-forward-c0u after PR #846. Delivers #805 R0-R5 without the authored catalog, Core behavior composer, or separate dev app.\n\n## Scope\n- Execute R0, R1, R2a, R2b, R3, R4, and R5 through independently reviewed PRs.\n- Maintain exact-cohort compatibility across Agent, Workspace, Core, CLI, plugin-cli, and full-app.\n\n## Constraints\n- One writer per overlapping Agent/Workspace/Core/CLI lane.\n- Every runtime/auth/session/plugin boundary gets standards, spec, and adversarial review.\n- R6 is product integration, not foundation completion.\n\n## Proof\n- R0-R5 proof artifacts and PRs linked.\n- Two configured agents share exact Workspace/Sandbox identity with isolated behavior.\n- Packed package and full-app compatibility pass.\n\n## Success Criteria\nAll R0-R5 children are closed and #805 foundation acceptance is satisfied.","acceptance_criteria":"All R0-R5 children are closed and #805 foundation acceptance is satisfied.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"deferred","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:34.972187808Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:00.998846057Z","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","a1","decision-26-superseded","workspace-agent"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:34.972187808Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:126:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.4.2","title":"R2b.2: migrate Core, MCP, automation, and trusted plugin consumers","description":"## Context\nRaw resolveWithWorkspace and `{workspaceId,userId}` dispatch paths are ambient authority and must be removed from hosted consumers.\n\n## Scope\n- Replace raw dispatcher resolver/APIs with the narrowed invocation facade.\n- Migrate Core route/service integration and default-only agent handoff.\n- Migrate full-app managed MCP, Agent MCP delegate/share/artifact reads, boring-automation hosted/manual/scheduled runs, ask-user, governance, and every stateful default plugin/trusted context.\n- Reauthorize queued/retry/auto-follow-up producers at start and each later status/result/artifact/cancel/session operation.\n- Keep public HTTP/UI/MCP routes free of agentTypeId.\n\n## Constraints\n- Consumer may retain only stable IDs/receipts.\n- Core cannot import authored source/plugin/prompt/tool/skill/Pi/harness composition.\n- No cross-app or non-member Workspace disclosure.\n\n## Proof\n- Repository gate for raw resolver/dispatcher/Workspace imports in affected consumers.\n- MCP and automation start/status/result/artifact/stop tests with mid-flight revocation.\n- Full-app compatibility suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nAll named consumers use the operation facade and no raw authorized Workspace remains in retained state.","acceptance_criteria":"All named consumers use the operation facade and no raw authorized Workspace remains in retained state.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"deferred","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:38.475897626Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:00.320757317Z","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","automation","core","decision-26-superseded","mcp","plugins","r2b"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.4.2","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.4","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:38.475897626Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.4.2","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.4.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:47.739219080Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:130:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.1","title":"R3.1: validate global agent definitions and Workspace-type policy","description":"## Context\nHost configuration, not plugins or Core, selects the allowed agents and trusted executable contributions.\n\n## Scope\n- Define/freeze one global definition per agentTypeId and one workspace-type default/allowed policy.\n- Require unique non-empty allowed set, default membership, exact authored definitionId equality, and installed canonical plugin IDs.\n- Cross-validate Core product types against Workspace policies at startup without exposing behavior to Core.\n- Group trusted server/package plugin surfaces by canonical ID and derive per-agent behavior view plus effective Workspace union.\n\n## Constraints\n- Plugins cannot enable themselves.\n- Routes/bridges/UI/assets stay host-global and self-authorizing for this shipment.\n- Model/provider policy remains existing host/session policy.\n\n## Proof\n- Startup validation/error matrix for duplicate/missing/default/ID/plugin/type mismatches.\n- Plugin canonical-order/provenance and route authorization tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nInvalid graphs fail before serving and valid policy deterministically selects default/allowed definitions and plugin views.","acceptance_criteria":"Invalid graphs fail before serving and valid policy deterministically selects default/allowed definitions and plugin views.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"deferred","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:39.433720831Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:00.200966472Z","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","decision-26-superseded","plugins","policy","r3"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.4.4","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:48.614010545Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:39.433720831Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:132:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.3","title":"R3.3: lazy typed bindings, capabilities contract, and failure isolation","description":"## Context\nWorkspace can now replace the primary-only binding with one lazy actor-neutral singleton per allowed type.\n\n## Scope\n- Add Map<agentTypeId, Promise<AgentBinding>> after current policy/allowed validation.\n- Compose each binding from current authored source, standard tools, and only its plugin behavior view against the shared runtime.\n- Isolate failed load cleanup/retry to that type; keep loaded bindings until runtime retirement.\n- Reload only currently loaded bindings plus shared provisioning and the requesting actor's selected live session.\n- Implement explicit Pi resource policy for configured hosts.\n- Ship exact capabilities migration: unchanged legacy unversioned primary or schemaVersion 2 authorized-workspace-default catalog; update explicit clients in the same cohort.\n\n## Constraints\n- Repeated lookup returns strict-equal binding.\n- Unknown/disallowed type never creates a promise.\n- Tool collisions stay deterministic, non-fatal, and diagnostic-driven.\n- No arbitrary type in public DTOs/routes.\n\n## Proof\n- Concurrent singleton, per-type failure/retry, shared runtime failure, reload loaded/unloaded, capability startup/authorization, and ambient Pi negative tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nTyped bindings are lazy, actor-neutral, failure-isolated, and expose only the server-selected default catalog publicly.","acceptance_criteria":"Typed bindings are lazy, actor-neutral, failure-isolated, and expose only the server-selected default catalog publicly.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"deferred","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.232971873Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:00.123914883Z","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","agent","capabilities","decision-26-superseded","r3"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.232971873Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:48.972928968Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:49.158545333Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:134:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","title":"R4: declarative authored-source correction and validate CLI","description":"## Context\nCorrect #814's unused published `0.1.90` authored catalog/tool semantics in one owner-approved, separately reviewed follow-up without rewriting history. Authored data becomes identity, safe metadata, and instructions only.\n\n## Scope\n- Simplify source/materialization, remove the unused published catalog contract, migrate repository callers/tests atomically, simplify validate, and prove packed consumption. No compatibility window or dedicated `0.2.0` boundary.\n\n## Constraints\n- May start after R0 only when no active R1-R3 Agent-package writer overlaps.\n- R0 found the public `0.1.90` surface; the owner confirmed no consumers and closed R4.0 with the corrective-follow-up strategy.\n\n## Proof\n- All R4 children and packed Agent/CLI proof pass.\n\n## Success Criteria\nNo authored executable selector remains and validation covers only declarative source.","acceptance_criteria":"No authored executable selector remains and validation covers only declarative source.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.678624166Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:01.625691894Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T21:18:20.342601217Z","close_reason":"R4 complete in one corrective follow-up: declarative authored source and validate CLI with no catalog runtime semantics; full Agent tests, focused CLI tests, builds, invariants, and packed consumer proof pass.","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","authoring","cli","decision-28-retained-evidence","decision-resolved","r4"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.678624166Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:135:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.1","title":"R4.1: simplify frozen authored source and remove catalog runtime semantics","description":"## Context\nThe authored source loader remains useful, but tools/skills/MCP/package/model/runtime policy belong to trusted host plugins and configuration.\n\n## Scope\n- Keep definitionId, schema version, label, description, and bounded instructions only.\n- Require host agentTypeId exactly equals source definitionId; aliases are forbidden.\n- Preserve contained import-free reads, UTF-8/size/count/path/symlink protections, deterministic frozen/redacted output, and no sibling executable import.\n- Reject non-empty legacy capability/tool/skill/MCP references with stable migration errors.\n- In one corrective PR, remove `AuthoredAgentToolCatalog`, `MaterializeAgentDirectoryInput.toolCatalog`, materialized `tools`/`declaredToolRefs`, authored capability/tool/skill/MCP ref fields, and catalog-only error paths; migrate repository callers/tests atomically.\n- Keep `materializeAgentDirectory` and `compileAgentDirectory` as simplified declarative operations; preserve unrelated compiler/digest/deployment exports and `AUTHORED_AGENT_TOOL_COLLISION` while normal composition uses it.\n\n## Constraints\n- Authored input never selects executable path/package/credential/command/model/plugin or runtime policy.\n- No forced rewrite of reviewed history.\n- R4.0 is closed: no compatibility window or dedicated `0.2.0` boundary; rollback is a normal revert before I0 publication.\n\n## Proof\n- Bounds/path/symlink/UTF-8/ID/legacy-ref matrix, executable sentinel, freeze/redaction, and source ID mismatch tests.\n- Package export/typecheck proof.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nMaterialized source is declarative-only and unsupported executable metadata cannot affect composition. The implementation matches the approved corrective scope and removes no HTTP/product endpoint or unrelated public export.","acceptance_criteria":"Materialized source is declarative-only and unsupported executable metadata cannot affect composition. The implementation matches the approved R4.0 public-API migration and target version.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"ubuntu","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.940953514Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:01.605865646Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T21:18:19.826666072Z","close_reason":"Implemented declarative-only authored source: removed catalog/tool-selector contracts, bounded race-checked no-symlink reads, safe metadata, frozen output, migration errors, tests, docs, and packed export proof.","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","agent","authoring","decision-28-retained-evidence","r4"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.940953514Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.3","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:50:21.933418626Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:136:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.2","title":"R4.2: simplify agent validate and prove packed Agent/CLI consumers","description":"## Context\nThe CLI validator must report the declarative contract and avoid resurrecting catalog/tool authority.\n\n## Scope\n- Before changing validate, add a direct regression that forces the generic fallback and locks redacted `INTERNAL_ERROR` / `agent validation failed`, empty stdout, JSON-or-human stderr, and exit code 1.\n- Simplify human and JSON success/error output to identity, metadata, instructions, bounds, and stable migration errors.\n- Remove/simplify success `agent.refs.{tools,capabilities,skills,mcpServers}` and corresponding human lines in the same corrective PR; migrate repository tests/callers atomically.\n- Pack/install Agent and CLI into an external fixture and run the real binary.\n- Document the owner finding (no consumers), corrective scope, and revert-before-I0 rollback.\n\n## Constraints\n- No tool catalog, package path, MCP command, model, credential, or plugin selector in output.\n- Redact local absolute paths and secret-like authored input.\n\n## Proof\n- Human/JSON golden tests, malformed/legacy cases, installed-bin validate smoke, packed import/exports, build/typecheck/invariants.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nPublished-shaped Agent/CLI consumers validate declarative sources with stable safe output.","acceptance_criteria":"Published-shaped Agent/CLI consumers validate declarative sources with stable safe output.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"ubuntu","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:41.137391665Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:01.583267277Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T21:18:20.171910699Z","close_reason":"Simplified agent validate to declarative metadata/instruction length, added stable legacy-ref and generic INTERNAL_ERROR redaction tests, and passed real packed Agent/CLI binary smoke.","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","cli","conformance","decision-28-retained-evidence","r4"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.2","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:41.137391665Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.2","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:49.635927977Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:138:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.7.1","title":"R5.1: implement one-shot and loopback agent dev on the regular server","description":"## Context\nDevelopers need fast authored-source feedback through the same production composition and lifecycle path.\n\n## Scope\n- Build clean launcher from current main and call createWorkspaceAgentServer directly.\n- Support one-shot capture and loopback serve as ingress/lifecycle differences only.\n- Use normal runtime, plugin, model, session, signal, listen, and close policy.\n- Ensure signal/listen failure cleanup is exact-once and errors are redacted.\n\n## Constraints\n- No createMaterializedAgentDevApp or second behavior composer.\n- No authored MCP/model/runtime executable selection.\n\n## Proof\n- One-shot/serve/regular-server capture equality for prompt/tools/skills/Pi invocation.\n- Signal, listen failure, close-once, redaction, and installed-bin dev tests.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nagent dev uses the ordinary server and differs only in chosen ingress/lifecycle.","acceptance_criteria":"agent dev uses the ordinary server and differs only in chosen ingress/lifecycle.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"deferred","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:41.631987985Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:00.016209693Z","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","cli","decision-26-superseded","dev","r5"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.7.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.5.4","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:49.799811576Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.7.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:49.936367793Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.7.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.7","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:41.631987985Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:141:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.2.1","title":"C1: CoreProductRequestScope and two-domain authentication topology","description":"## Context\nReplace retired AgentHost deployment fields in typed products with exact host-derived product scope while preserving ordinary full-app hosts.\n\n## Scope\n- Define frozen Core product domain and workspace declarations.\n- Normalize exact hostname under explicit trusted proxy rules and resolve expected workspaceTypeId plus create policy before authentication without disclosing Workspaces.\n- Make typed product scope and legacy deployment scope startup-mutually-exclusive; remove agent/deployment identity from the typed request scope.\n- Cross-check Core product workspace types against Workspace host policy at startup.\n- Prove cookies, origin, CSRF, logout, signup/login, and proxy behavior across two domains.\n\n## Constraints\n- Scope cannot carry workspaceId or agent identity and never authorizes membership.\n- Unknown domains fail closed only for typed-domain hosts; localhost/preview/full-app compatibility remains explicit.\n- No implicit Workspace creation on login/signup.\n\n## Proof\n- Hostname spoof/proxy/port/case/IDNA matrix, startup graph failures, two-domain browser/server auth proof, and full-app compatibility.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nCore derives only trusted expected product type/create policy and authentication behaves correctly on both domains.","acceptance_criteria":"Core derives only trusted expected product type/create policy and authentication behaves correctly on both domains.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"deferred","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:42.314918405Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:12:59.762261342Z","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","auth","c1","core","decision-26-superseded","domain"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.2.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.2","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:42.314918405Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:146:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.3.1","title":"R6.1: replace Seneca #16 with declarative sources and trusted plugins","description":"## Context\nBuild the product integration from current Seneca main rather than merging the superseded catalog/dev-app branch.\n\n## Scope\n- Pin the exact Boring Agent/Workspace/Core/CLI cohort.\n- Define two Core product domain/type declarations and matching Workspace default/allowed policies with global declarative agent sources and trusted Seneca plugins.\n- Keep one human default per product while backend fixture proves two allowed agents share one runtime.\n- Use trusted idempotent one-shot host script to seed dedicated company/customer Workspace context where required; do not reconcile later edits continuously.\n- Supersede Seneca #16 with linked replacement PR.\n\n## Constraints\n- No authored executable refs or plugin self-enablement.\n- Dedicated isolation requires explicit separate Workspace.\n- No public agent selector or delegated multi-agent product.\n\n## Proof\n- Seneca typecheck/tests/build/image, exact pin verification, two-domain auth/type negatives, shared-runtime fixture, session/restart proof.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nReplacement Seneca PR is reviewable, exact-pinned, and demonstrates both products without superseded architecture.","acceptance_criteria":"Replacement Seneca PR is reviewable, exact-pinned, and demonstrates both products without superseded architecture.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"deferred","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:43.418419074Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:12:59.640760853Z","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","decision-26-superseded","r6","seneca"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.3.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.2.4","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:51.039776380Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.3.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.3","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:43.418419074Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.3.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.3.3","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:17:05.312009066Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:157:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.3","title":"R4.0 gate: approve migration for published authored APIs","description":"## Context\nR0 proved that the #813-#815 authored APIs are not unpublished implementation details: `@hachej/boring-agent@0.1.90` publicly exports `materializeAgentDirectory`, `MaterializedAgentSourceV1`, `AuthoredAgentToolCatalog`, and catalog-related errors, while `@hachej/boring-ui-cli@0.1.90` ships `agent validate` and its schema-v1 output. R4 cannot remove or silently repurpose those contracts without an explicit release/migration decision.\n\n## Scope\n- Choose and document the compatibility strategy for the published 0.1.90 surface: coordinated breaking 0.2 release, deprecation/compatibility window plus a new declarative API, or another explicitly versioned migration.\n- Decide treatment of `tools`, `declaredToolRefs`, `toolCatalog`, catalog error codes, old definition ref arrays, and validate JSON/human fields.\n- Specify consumer migration for registry users, repository callers, golden-path timing, and superseded Seneca #16.\n- Mark every adjacent public compiler, definition, digest, validation, and deployment export listed in `R0-AUDIT.md` as preserve unchanged or define its versioned migration; preserve or separately migrate `AUTHORED_AGENT_TOOL_COLLISION` for the live normal tool composer.\n- Set the minimum rollback floor and whether I0 may publish the chosen break.\n- Update R4.1/R4.2 acceptance and docs before implementation.\n\n## Constraints\n- No direct R4 removal or semantic repurposing before this gate closes.\n- Stable errors/fields remain stable unless the approved version boundary and migration notes say otherwise.\n- The active runtime still must end with declarative authored identity/metadata/instructions only; compatibility must not reintroduce authored executable authority.\n\n## Proof\n- Registry declarations and integrity for Agent/CLI 0.1.90.\n- Public export/CLI field matrix from the R0 audit.\n- Written owner decision with target version, migration examples, package cohort, and rollback floor.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nOwner approves one explicit semver/migration strategy for every published authored surface, and R4.1/R4.2 are updated so implementation cannot silently break or preserve the wrong contract.\n\n## Owner decision — 2026-07-20\n- Confirmed: there are no consumers of the superseded authored catalog/materializer/validate surface.\n- Implement one separately reviewed corrective R4 follow-up PR; do not create a compatibility window or a dedicated `0.2.0` boundary.\n- Remove catalog/tool-selector authority and simplify validate; migrate all repository callers/tests atomically in that PR.\n- Preserve unrelated compiler/digest/deployment exports and preserve `AUTHORED_AGENT_TOOL_COLLISION` while normal tool composition uses it. No HTTP or product endpoint is removed.\n- Keep #816/#817 and Seneca #16 superseded; do not merge them as compatibility.\n- Rollback floor: revert the corrective PR before I0 publication. I0 still chooses and human-approves the later joint package cohort.\n","acceptance_criteria":"Owner approves one explicit semver/migration strategy for every published authored surface, and R4.1/R4.2 are updated so implementation cannot silently break or preserve the wrong contract.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:50:21.269805096Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:01.649393101Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T19:46:58.165031036Z","close_reason":"Owner approved one corrective R4 follow-up: no consumers, no compatibility window or dedicated 0.2.0 boundary; atomic repository migration; preserve unrelated exports/product APIs.","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","decision-28-retained-evidence","decision-recorded","r4"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:50:21.636503637Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:50:21.269805096Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:158:{"id":"wt-391-forward-16f.1","title":"16f.1 BYOK credential-injection CONTRACT + provider-registry seam","description":"Contract-first, ships in v1. Land the typed secret-reference + (workspaceId,providerId)->credential resolve interface and the provider registry seam: versioned provider/field/ref/resolver/opaque-authority(WorkspaceCredentialAuthorityVerifierV1)/lease/error types, the (deferred-Tier-2) SandboxCredential payload/callback/receipt types, host-owned trust/delivery rules, and the Tier-1 HOST-SIDE RESOLUTION path (trusted first-party => delivery host-only; key never enters sandbox). No storage, no wire implementation, no plaintext.\n\nTHIS bead is the seam SBX1.1 (#855) reconciles its stub against: SBX1.1 stubs the ref/resolver callback now and the vault implementation (16f.2/16f.5) lands behind it. Owner-ratified 2026-07-20 (amendments A/D/E) per docs/issues/820/byok-secret-vault-plan.md.\n\nAcceptance gates (plan 'Contract and registry'): a standalone SBX1 fake compiles against this, accepts a typed reference/delivery request + fake payload-resolver callback, rejects model/host-only delivery into sandbox, validates bounded payload identities, emits a value-free receipt, returns stable CREDENTIAL_* errors without importing a vault/store impl; registry tests validate every provider/field ID, OAuth URL/scope, consumer binding, host-assigned trust/purpose/allowed-field/delivery/channel/egress at startup; OAuth registry rejects missing/public/duplicate/oversized refresh/access fields and bindings cannot request the refresh field; external-managed rejects token fields and non-host delivery; tenant input/model output/command text cannot create or widen a reference; package import invariants remain green (shared has no node:*/Buffer, workspace base has zero Agent value imports).","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-20T21:01:27.776172274Z","created_by":"claude-opus","updated_at":"2026-07-22T05:00:00.000000000Z","source_repo":"wt-820-beads","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/wt-820-beads","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","820"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-16f.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-16f","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T21:01:27.776172274Z","created_by":"claude-opus","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:163:{"id":"wt-391-forward-16f.6","title":"16f.6 (DEFERRED) BYOK in-sandbox injection (Tier-2, untrusted custom tools)","description":"DEFERRED (amendment D). The ONLY path that delivers a secret INTO the sandbox, for untrusted tenant custom tools (tenant 'user repo' code needing a credential). Delivery via stdin/pipe (FD 3) or per-execution tmpfs; NEVER env/argv/image/common-create-context. Not built in v1; deferred until a tenant actually authors a credential-using custom tool. GATED behind (a) a hostile-test harness (plant a canary secret; assert it never appears in sandbox env, /proc/*/environ, ps, argv, docker inspect/config/labels, image/history/layers, durable /workspace, logs; assert a cross-workspace probe cannot read another workspace's injected secret; mirror the runsc qualification-harness approach) PLUS (b) a red-team pass on the contract before implementation. Pairs with SBX1 wt-391-forward-6gd.3 for concrete worker-to-child FD3/tmpfs delivery + teardown.\n\nAcceptance gates (plan 'Sandbox delivery'): two-workspace x two-sandbox cross-product rejects mismatched refs before decrypt; authenticated sandboxId<->workspaceId receipt mandatory; canary available only on FD3/fixed-tmpfs to the intended process and absent from every sink above; success/provider-error/handler-error/timeout/abort/fork/double-fork/worker-disconnect all close/unmount/clear and uncertain cleanup destroys the container and blocks reuse; remains disabled under network-none until per-provider egress + fresh SBX1 isolation/exfiltration qualification pass; positive control proves the intended tenant process can read its own credential and call only the allowed fake endpoint.","notes":"DESIGN GUIDANCE (from sandbox-provider injection research, 2026-07-22): The in-sandbox delivery mechanism for Tier-2 should follow the industry standard, which corrects an earlier 'prefer stdin/tmpfs' note. BASELINE = env-var-at-creation, per-workspace, injected from the control-plane vault at sandbox boot — this is what E2B, Modal, Vercel (our current sandbox), Fly, and Cloudflare all do. Env vars are acceptable here because the sandbox is single-tenant and the secret belongs to that tenant; cross-tenant safety rests ENTIRELY on gVisor isolation strength (the SBX1.2 qualification), NOT on env-var hiding. OWASP's 'no secrets in env vars' targets shared multi-app hosts and does not apply to a single-tenant isolated sandbox where the sandbox owner = secret owner. PREMIUM OPTION (evaluate for the external-service/standalone-sandbox tier where the code author is NOT the key owner): Daytona-style egress-proxy brokering — the env var holds an opaque PLACEHOLDER and the real value is substituted at the network egress proxy for allow-listed hosts, so the key never enters the sandbox and code cannot read/exfiltrate it. This is the correct form of a 'vault broker' (swap-at-egress, not fetch-from-inside). CAVEATS to design around: (1) the daemon/injector sees plaintext at boot — minimize the trusted injector, scope decryption to boot, drop access on teardown (Fly model); store keys encrypted at rest in the control-plane vault (KMS envelope), never in images/snapshots; (2) env persists for the sandbox lifetime and is readable by any code run — accepted for BYOK (tenant's own key = residual #7), but for untrusted-to-the-tenant code use the egress-proxy; (3) persistent/snapshotted sandboxes (Vercel persistence is default) may capture env state — EXCLUDE secrets from snapshots or re-inject at resume. Still gated behind the canary/leak-invariant hostile-test harness + red-team before implementation.","status":"deferred","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-20T21:02:10.839093403Z","created_by":"claude-opus","updated_at":"2026-07-22T05:32:06.003594048Z","source_repo":"wt-820-beads","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/wt-820-beads","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","820","deferred"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-16f.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-16f","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T21:02:10.839093403Z","created_by":"claude-opus","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-16f.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-16f.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T21:02:23.026411084Z","created_by":"claude-opus","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:165:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.5","title":"F0a: ratify Decision-28 authority and replacement Bead graph","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Context and scope\nDecision 26 and old R1-R6/C1-C4/I1 are rejected. Closed R0/R4 remain evidence. #844 landed compatibility `workspaceTypeId`; #845 head `e6bd0e7239eea85ed8ce867c7326a28fc2531fec` is green but semantically wrong.\n- Merge Decision 28 and canonical #391/#805 plans, uniform historical banners, proof/ownership/mode/roadmap docs, and golden-path gates.\n- Record #845 reviewed head/base and file-level salvage/recreate/discard destinations before closure. Keep hostname/proxy/cookie/Origin/CSRF/browser ideas; reject typed-Workspace routing/API mode.\n- Recut this epic to F-series; defer old open descendants without deletion; retain closed R0/R4; create H2c/H8 and deferred H4a.\n- Converge four plan/spec/architecture reviews and compact owner-authorized Fable rounds. No runtime implementation.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nF0A-PLAN-PROOF/PR proof records authority diff, changed-link and stale-authority scans, `git diff --check`, golden path, `br lint`, `br dep cycles`, `bv --robot-insights`, reviews, #845 ledger and Bead map. No implementation dispatch before this authority PR merges.\n## Review\nProduct architecture, plan/spec, thermo, Fable.\n## Rollback\nDocs/tracker revert only; never restore Decision-26 semantics.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"F0A-PLAN-PROOF/PR proof records authority diff, changed-link and stale-authority scans, `git diff --check`, golden path, `br lint`, `br dep cycles`, `bv --robot-insights`, reviews, #845 ledger and Bead map. No implementation dispatch before this authority PR merges.","notes":"Final Fable R3 verdict READY after Oracle R4 localized fixes. Durable proof and PR #845 file-level ledger: docs/issues/805/runtime-refactor/work/A1-agent-authoring/F0A-PLAN-PROOF.md. Keep in_progress until authority PR merges; do not dispatch F0b before merge.","status":"in_progress","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:36.423782979Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:28:35.851014696Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","beads","decision-28","planning"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.5","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:36.423782979Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:166:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","title":"F0b: refresh current-main consumer, provider, publication, and migration inventory","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nRefresh retained R0 on merged F0a. Inventory every live read/write/edit/list/stat/mkdir/delete/move/find/grep/watch/exec consumer; provisioning/path/plugin/UI/CLI surface; package export/peer/registry/pack consumer; composition root; provider mechanic; session store; current-main #844 row/API behavior; #845 salvage. Distinguish current main from unmerged branches. Ground each fact in file/symbol or reproducible package evidence and assign F1-F8b owner.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n`F0B-INVENTORY.md/.json` are complete and machine-readable with zero unowned path; package/tarball facts reproduce; changed links/authority and diff checks pass.\n## Review\nCode-grounding and package architecture.\n## Rollback\nEvidence-only no-op; supersede with newer dated inventory.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"`F0B-INVENTORY.md/.json` are complete and machine-readable with zero unowned path; package/tarball facts reproduce; changed links/authority and diff checks pass.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:36.814449238Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:33.047836014Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","architecture","audit"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:36.814449238Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.1","type":"related","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:50.803494418Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","type":"related","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:50.993095952Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.5","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:45.186817659Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:167:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.7","title":"F1a: freeze Environment operation and logical-binding contract","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nIn boring-bash/shared define transport-neutral read/write/edit/list/stat/mkdir/delete/move/find/grep/watch/exec, bounds, stable errors, cancellation/local-watch. Admission carries logical filesystem IDs/access/projection/constrained virtual destination—never raw roots. Server `CanonicalFilesystemResolver` maps authorized Workspace+logical ID; only provider adapters derive paths. No node/Buffer/Fastify/Agent/Workspace/provider values in shared. Add fakes/compat aliases additively.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nAPI snapshot/fake conformance covers every op, malformed/bounded inputs, cancellation, anti-forgery/no raw roots and watch lifecycle. Boring-bash test/typecheck/build + common gates; `F1A-CONTRACT-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nEnvironment API and security.\n## Rollback\nUnused additive exports revert before migration.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"API snapshot/fake conformance covers every op, malformed/bounded inputs, cancellation, anti-forgery/no raw roots and watch lifecycle. Boring-bash test/typecheck/build + common gates; `F1A-CONTRACT-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:37.213999140Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:44.728490208Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","api","boring-bash","environment","security","security-review-required"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.7","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:37.213999140Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.7","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:45.423750694Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:168:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.8","title":"F1b: freeze Environment admission, lifecycle, grants, and host-root ports","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nSeparate service-derived reusable backend key from authority-bearing invocation view bound to Workspace/environment/actor/Agent/session/invocation/ops/logical bindings/governance/network/expiry/cancellation/trust class. Specify acquire-stage-publish-drain-refcount-release-invalidate; expiry rejects new work, bounded-cancels in-flight, release idempotent. Define one-exec unforgeable `ExecutionGrantBroker`; secrets never admission/lease/filesystem/session/log/cache/global env. Separately define consumer-injected `ModelCapabilityIssuer`; Workspace requests one opaque client after auth and AgentApp never caches credentials. Name web/CLI host-root and provider eligibility ports.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nState/race/property/hostile tests cover failure cleanup, atomic publish, expiry/drain/refcount, ignored cancellation, cross-view isolation, one-use grants, model/shell separation and non-caller trust class. Boring-bash gates; `F1B-LIFECYCLE-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nSecurity and lifecycle.\n## Rollback\nAdditive ports/fakes revert; no persisted lease/credential state.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"State/race/property/hostile tests cover failure cleanup, atomic publish, expiry/drain/refcount, ignored cancellation, cross-view isolation, one-use grants, model/shell separation and non-caller trust class. Boring-bash gates; `F1B-LIFECYCLE-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:37.594905577Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:44.728490208Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","boring-bash","capabilities","lifecycle","security","security-review-required"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.8","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:37.594905577Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.8","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.7","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:45.583007250Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:169:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.9","title":"F2a: neutralize Sandbox backend contract and ratify provider enforcement","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nReplace final Agent-owned Workspace/Sandbox provider boundary with neutral backend handle for provisioning, canonical storage, exec, physical bindings, health/invalidation, persistence/cleanup; retain old exports during expansion. Ratify direct/bwrap/Vercel source of truth, locality, ops, physical binding/network, durability/watch/eligibility from code/tests. Every requirement is physical/advisory/unsupported. Hosted requires physical and fails stable unsupported when absent; direct/advisory is trusted-local unrestricted only. Remote staging may seed but never hide sync.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nProvider matrix + hostile tests prove actual mechanics, neutral imports, Vercel canonical-data ruling, direct/bwrap negatives and hosted network fail-closed. Sandbox test/typecheck/build + common gates; `F2A-PROVIDER-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nProvider, thermo, security.\n## Rollback\nOld exports/selection stay; no canonical data mutation.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Provider matrix + hostile tests prove actual mechanics, neutral imports, Vercel canonical-data ruling, direct/bwrap negatives and hosted network fail-closed. Sandbox test/typecheck/build + common gates; `F2A-PROVIDER-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:38.100511792Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:32.360613242Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","boring-sandbox","providers","security-review-required"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:38.100511792Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:4