origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:170:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.10","title":"F2b-i: implement local boring-bash Environment service","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nImplement boring-bash/server canonical resolver, all ops, invocation views, exact-fact backend reuse, fail-toward-isolation, refs/drain/expiry/cancel, provider adapters, one-exec grants, stable errors and cleanup while old consumers remain switchable. Narrow views never reuse broader namespaces/wrappers/process env/grants.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nConformance covers all ops, file/exec coherence, resolver authority, view separation, grant redemption, lifecycle races, ignored cancellation, stage failure cleanup and no partial publish. Bash+Sandbox gates; `F2B-I-SERVICE-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nService, security, lifecycle.\n## Rollback\nSwitch to old path and dispose manager; no copy/rewrite.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Conformance covers all ops, file/exec coherence, resolver authority, view separation, grant redemption, lifecycle races, ignored cancellation, stage failure cleanup and no partial publish. Bash+Sandbox gates; `F2B-I-SERVICE-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:38.457271234Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:44.728490208Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","boring-bash","environment","lifecycle","security","security-review-required"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.10","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:38.457271234Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.10","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.9","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:46.001944855Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:171:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.11","title":"F2b-ii: migrate every Environment consumer and prove provider coherence","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nMigrate every F0b Agent tool, Workspace file/status/watch adapter, bash route, CLI path, plugin, provisioning, search/path consumer to EnvironmentService. Remove bypasses; retain transition exports until H2c. One actor sees immediate one-filesystem coherence across tools/exec/UI/CLI; no host-sandbox sync or per-Agent canonical copy. Unsupported ops/providers reject, never degrade.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nZero unapproved old paths. Per-provider matrix covers every op, file/exec coherence, readonly/readwrite/absent shell, hostile IDs/paths, unsupported op/network, lifecycle and persistence. Bash/Sandbox/Agent/Workspace/CLI suites + common; `F2B-II-MIGRATION-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nMigration and service/security.\n## Rollback\nConsumer switches to retained adapters; never copy/rewrite data.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Zero unapproved old paths. Per-provider matrix covers every op, file/exec coherence, readonly/readwrite/absent shell, hostile IDs/paths, unsupported op/network, lifecycle and persistence. Bash/Sandbox/Agent/Workspace/CLI suites + common; `F2B-II-MIGRATION-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:38.821149950Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:44.728490208Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","conformance","environment","migration","security","security-review-required"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.11","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:38.821149950Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.11","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.10","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:46.242404490Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:172:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","title":"F3a: add dedicated AgentApplication entrypoint and static fleet validator","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nPublish server-neutral `@hachej/boring-agent/application` with AgentApplication.invoke, immutable identity/version, invocation/session/model/Environment context, result/factory. No Fastify/UI/Core/CLI/Workspace implementation/provider values or front import. Workspace server owns and validates the frozen fleet grammar while importing the Agent application API: unique exact agentTypeId==definitionId, application default, trusted source/plugin-role references, no authored executable catalogs, no eager Workspace/App/Environment/model/backend. Host and CLI adapters compile to that one Workspace validator; Agent does not own a second fleet registry. Add ModelCapabilityIssuer port/fakes and opaque per-call model capability; hosted issuer F5a, CLI F6.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nTests cover invalid/duplicate IDs, missing default/ref/role, freeze/copy, eager negatives, pack/import direction and no credential capture. Agent test/typecheck/build + clean tarball + common; `F3A-APPLICATION-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nAgent API/package layering.\n## Rollback\nAdditive entrypoint unused until cutover.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Tests cover invalid/duplicate IDs, missing default/ref/role, freeze/copy, eager negatives, pack/import direction and no credential capture. Agent test/typecheck/build + clean tarball + common; `F3A-APPLICATION-PROOF.md`. Workspace owns the sole fleet validator; Agent exposes only the application API and CLI does not embed another validator.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:39.204171791Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:31.517081616Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","agent","agent-application","fleet","package-api"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:39.204171791Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:46.526117725Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:173:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.13","title":"F4a: add hosted default persistence and correct #844 semantics","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nAdd nullable workspaces.default_agent_type_id; no DB NOT NULL. Distinguish missing row, legacy null, non-null. Atomic new Workspace+owner membership+validated default. Ordinary uses application default; signup only pre-reserved mapped default. Legacy-null CAS application default only; no update API. Keep migration 0023 immutable and make workspaceTypeId inert in routing/membership/selection/creation/Agent/session/provisioning/cache. Audit data; non-default semantics stop and activate H4a—never coerce.\nNon-null writer lands dark until stored-default-aware serving/rollback honors value or disables execution. Metadata-ignorant cohort is pre-write schema probe only.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nForward/old reader-writer/rollback matrix covers missing/null/non-null/CAS/atomicity/no NOT NULL/inert workspaceTypeId; audit and writer activation fence proven. Core/Workspace gates; `F4A-MIGRATION-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nMigration/Core persistence/rollback.\n## Rollback\nOld cohort serves only pre-write. After writes, honor type or disable; never map.\n## Conditional gate\nIf audit triggers, make H4a active and blocker, then add owner-approved migration node.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Forward/old reader-writer/rollback matrix covers missing/null/non-null/CAS/atomicity/no NOT NULL/inert workspaceTypeId; audit and writer activation fence proven. Core/Workspace gates; `F4A-MIGRATION-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:39.591553234Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:33.780605793Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","core","migration","security-review-required","workspace"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.13","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:39.591553234Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.13","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:46.713992625Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:174:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.14","title":"F4b: implement local registry locking and acting-Agent session metadata","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nHost-neutral local registry store: atomic write, single-writer process lock, revision/mtime conflict, stale owner/liveness, crash recovery, compatible-field preservation, stable conflicts. This is local entry protection, not deployment publication CAS. Registry owns Workspace identity/default; fleet YAML has no per-Workspace state. Add acting agentTypeId to hosted/local durable sessions. Legacy session uses persisted Workspace default; malformed/removed fails execution without hiding history. No CLI composition.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nMulti-process lost-update/stale/crash/revision/schema tests and hosted/local session roundtrip/history/delete/drift/old-cohort tolerance. Workspace/CLI gates; `F4B-PERSISTENCE-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nSessions/CLI persistence/concurrency.\n## Rollback\nPreserve additive values; old reader may ignore not rewrite; honor type or disable.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Multi-process lost-update/stale/crash/revision/schema tests and hosted/local session roundtrip/history/delete/drift/old-cohort tolerance. Workspace/CLI gates; `F4B-PERSISTENCE-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:39.999272275Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:32.628874907Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","cli","persistence","sessions","workspace"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.14","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:39.999272275Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.14","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:46.972866020Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:175:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.15","title":"F3b-i: build Workspace single-Agent orchestrator on real Environment service","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nWorkspace API accepts consumer-authorized context, not paths. Resolve persisted default; null/malformed/missing fails before Environment. Request consumer model capability, compile trusted governance, acquire scoped Environment, route/create acting-Agent session, invoke one AgentApplication, queue/cancel/emit and clean all failures. Owned history/list/attachments/delete/file/status use Agent-independent Workspace admission and remain available when Agent unavailable, still through EnvironmentService—not second filesystem.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nIntegration covers web/local context, default/model/Environment ordering, sessions, Agent-independent paths, queue/cancel and every failure cleanup/stable error. Agent/Workspace/Bash gates; `F3B-I-ORCHESTRATOR-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nAuthority/lifecycle.\n## Rollback\nDisable invocation or use stored-default-aware compatible path.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Integration covers web/local context, default/model/Environment ordering, sessions, Agent-independent paths, queue/cancel and every failure cleanup/stable error. Agent/Workspace/Bash gates; `F3B-I-ORCHESTRATOR-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:40.411165210Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:44.728490208Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","authorization","lifecycle","orchestration","security-review-required","workspace"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.15","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:40.411165210Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.15","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.11","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:47.146051188Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.15","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:47.390357714Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.15","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.13","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:47.636214168Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.15","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.14","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:47.808462381Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:176:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.16","title":"F3b-ii: generation-safe AgentApplication lifecycle and internal two-Agent seam","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nActor-neutral lazy registry keyed Workspace+fleet/plugin generation+Agent type; never cache actor/session/model/Environment. Single-flight load, failed-load retry, generation swap, bounded drain/dispose, idempotent release, concurrent sessions. Add package-internal conformance-only Workspace operation selecting validated fleet member under already-authorized context through identical session/governance/model/Environment pipeline. No public selector/UX/remote/stable external contract.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nRace/property tests cover load/retry/generation/drain/dispose/concurrent leak isolation; two real Apps execute internal full path and cannot bypass authority. Agent/Workspace gates; `F3B-II-LIFECYCLE-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nConcurrency/session isolation.\n## Rollback\nDrain generation; F3b-i default only.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Race/property tests cover load/retry/generation/drain/dispose/concurrent leak isolation; two real Apps execute internal full path and cannot bypass authority. Agent/Workspace gates; `F3B-II-LIFECYCLE-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:40.856145685Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:44.728490208Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","agent","concurrency","lifecycle","multi-agent","security-review-required","workspace"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.16","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:40.856145685Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.16","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.15","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:48.038456417Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:177:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.17","title":"F5a: compose Core/web consumer, signup intent, and hosted model issuer","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nCore/web independently consumes Workspace: authenticate+membership every operation; inject persistence/model/provider roots; never load Agent behavior. Signup validates trusted proxy/exact host, maps fleet default, durably reserves bounded expiring intent bound nonce/app/Agent before auth-user side effect, binds created user, atomically creates Workspace+owner+default, retires intent. Login cannot recover; conflict/orphan operator state; retry cannot change default; removed Agent terminal.\nHosted issuer after membership: readable Workspace BYOK wins; absent BYOK uses only explicit ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; both absent stable fail; unreadable BYOK fails without fallback; ambient Pi/OAuth never fallback. Opaque per-call client only.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nIsolated Postgres membership/atomic crash table at reserve/user/bind/Workspace/retire; hostile retry/orphan/conflict/removed Agent; full Decision-27 key matrix/non-capture. Clean packed Core+Workspace has no CLI. Core/Workspace gates; `F5A-WEB-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nAuth/transaction/security.\n## Rollback\nDisable signup initializer; honor stored defaults or disable.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Isolated Postgres membership/atomic crash table at reserve/user/bind/Workspace/retire; hostile retry/orphan/conflict/removed Agent; full Decision-27 key matrix/non-capture. Clean packed Core+Workspace has no CLI. Core/Workspace gates; `F5A-WEB-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:41.186479563Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:31.196553819Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","auth","core","security-review-required","signup"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.17","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:41.186479563Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.17","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.16","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:48.221022724Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:178:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.18","title":"F5b: recreate sibling auth security proof and supersede PR #845","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nRecreate from current main #845's exact host normalization, malformed/duplicate rejection, bounded proxy, PSL-safe cookie parent, HTTPS Origins, CSRF/redirect, shared logout, config failures and real Better Auth browser proof. Do not wholesale cherry-pick. Remove Workspace-type routing/portfolio/type graph/API mode/domain authority. Reconcile F0a head/base file ledger and close/supersede #845.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nHost/Forwarded/Origin/redirect/cookie/logout tests; isolated Postgres Better Auth and Chromium proof with cleanup on all failures. Core/full-app gates; `F5B-AUTH-PROOF.md` + #845 disposition.\n## Review\nIndependent web security.\n## Rollback\nRevert auth adapter without identity/default mutation.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Host/Forwarded/Origin/redirect/cookie/logout tests; isolated Postgres Better Auth and Chromium proof with cleanup on all failures. Core/full-app gates; `F5B-AUTH-PROOF.md` + #845 disposition.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:41.623494786Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:31.312021413Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","auth","browser","core","security-review-required"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.18","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:41.623494786Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.18","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.17","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:48.493921801Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:179:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.19","title":"F6: compose independent CLI fleet/Workspace consumer and regular agent dev","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nCLI separately reads trusted fleet YAML and local registry state, compiles same fleet, chooses trusted-local actor/root, injects neutral providers and local ModelCapabilityIssuer, consumes Workspace with no Core import/process/HTTP. New Workspace uses app default unless named creation initializer selects fleet member once under F4b lock; never mutate existing non-null. Folder/workspaces/one-shot/serve/regular agent dev share registry/orchestrator. Preserve fields/conflicts/history/cleanup.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nFleet-vs-registry schema, invalid IDs, initializer immutability, lock/revision/crash, mode parity, model isolation, Ctrl-C/failure, restart/session/drift. Clean packed CLI+Workspace no Core/source fallback. CLI/Workspace gates; `F6-CLI-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nCLI/package/concurrency.\n## Rollback\nPreserve state; disable rather than reinterpret.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Fleet-vs-registry schema, invalid IDs, initializer immutability, lock/revision/crash, mode parity, model isolation, Ctrl-C/failure, restart/session/drift. Clean packed CLI+Workspace no Core/source fallback. CLI/Workspace gates; `F6-CLI-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:42.060729073Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:30.615039051Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","cli","concurrency","dev","workspace"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.19","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:42.060729073Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.19","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.16","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:48.681041783Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:180:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.20","title":"F7: prove two-Agent governance, canonical data, and leak isolation","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nTwo real fleet Apps in one authorized Workspace via F3b-ii internal path. Prove one no-copy filesystem across Apps/tools/shell/UI/CLI; narrow views; physical readonly/readwrite/absent; op/network eligibility; backend reuse exact facts but distinct authority; refcount/restart/drain/generation/removed default/session; no actor/Agent/session/invocation shell-secret/model/session/credential/cancel leakage.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nMatrix covers every op, immediate coherence, hostile paths, shell/network negatives, concurrent views/ref release, one-exec reuse rejection, model non-capture, history with unavailable Agent, restart/drift. Six package/pack suites + common; `F7-CONFORMANCE-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nThermo and governance/security.\n## Rollback\nNo migration; failure blocks contraction/publication.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Matrix covers every op, immediate coherence, hostile paths, shell/network negatives, concurrent views/ref release, one-exec reuse rejection, model non-capture, history with unavailable Agent, restart/drift. Six package/pack suites + common; `F7-CONFORMANCE-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:42.420743950Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:34.102515664Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","conformance","multi-agent","security-review-required"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.20","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:42.420743950Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.20","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.18","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:48.950200637Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.20","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.19","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:49.257053664Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:181:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.21","title":"H2c Human Intention: approve exact compatibility contraction and file deletions","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Decision\nAfter green F7, review exact obsolete files/exports, repo+pack audit, pinned default-aware restoration cohort and F2c plan. Approve only named WorkspaceSandboxPairV1/Bash runtime bundle/provider edge deletion. Repository hard rule requires explicit written permission. Rejection/change returns to plan; no mutation in gate.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nHuman decision names files/exports, compatibility break, SHA, restoration integrity and scope in Bead/Inbox.\n## Review\nOwner compatibility/deletion.\n## Rollback\nNo-op gate.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Human decision names files/exports, compatibility break, SHA, restoration integrity and scope in Bead/Inbox.","status":"open","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:42.816801788Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:30.829394828Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","compatibility","deletion","human-intention","ready-for-human"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.21","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:42.816801788Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.21","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.20","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:49.454770642Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:182:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.22","title":"F2c: contract only owner-approved Agent-coupled Environment exports","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nAfter H2c remove/contract only approved WorkspaceSandboxPairV1, Agent-coupled Bash bundle and provider edges. Update manifests/docs/import audits: Sandbox no Agent/Workspace values; Bash sole Environment boundary. Preserve approved compatibility cohort. No publication.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nZero unapproved obsolete imports/exports; clean packed six-package consumers pass. `F2C-CONTRACTION-PROOF.md` links H2c and exact diff; all package/common gates.\n## Review\nCompatibility/final thermo.\n## Rollback\nOnly pinned default-aware cohort; never pre-fleet mapping.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Zero unapproved obsolete imports/exports; clean packed six-package consumers pass. `F2C-CONTRACTION-PROOF.md` links H2c and exact diff; all package/common gates.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:43.200785671Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:34.217002631Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","boring-bash","boring-sandbox","compatibility","contraction"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.22","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:43.200785671Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.22","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.21","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:49.695078263Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:183:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.23","title":"F8a: qualify contracted packed release candidate and Seneca rollback","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nFrom clean merged post-F2c SHA build exact contracted cohort. Test installed Core-only, CLI-only, combined full-app and Seneca with two signup hosts/defaults; membership, restart, acting-Agent history/delete, Environment coherence, unavailable Agent and pinned default-aware rollback. Packed only/no links/source. Do not publish.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n`F8A-RELEASE-CANDIDATE-PROOF.md` records SHA/version/integrity/scans/fixtures/commands/two defaults/restart/session/rollback/no fallback. Full-app test/typecheck/build/e2e + common.\n## Review\nRelease/product/final architecture/security.\n## Rollback\nPinned cohort honors defaults or disables.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"`F8A-RELEASE-CANDIDATE-PROOF.md` records SHA/version/integrity/scans/fixtures/commands/two defaults/restart/session/rollback/no fallback. Full-app test/typecheck/build/e2e + common.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:43.571901645Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:33.898384229Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","packages","release-candidate","security-review-required","seneca"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.23","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:43.571901645Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.23","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.22","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:49.857029842Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
