ease.\n## Rollback\nNo-op gate.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Human decision names SHA/versions/integrity/target/rollback/time in Bead/Inbox.","status":"open","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:44.045345757Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:33.399147424Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","human-intention","ready-for-human","release"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.24","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:44.045345757Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.24","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.23","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:50.111776777Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:185:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.25","title":"F8b: publish approved cohort and prove clean Seneca production install","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nPublish only H8 cohort via repo path. Empty-cache Core/CLI/full-app/Seneca install from registry with lock integrity and no workspace/link/file/local/cache/source fallback. Run imports/bins/plugins and post-release two-default membership/restart/session/history/Environment/unavailable-Agent smoke; record provenance; close delivery. Do not start deferred MCP/UX/remote/contracted work.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n`F8B-PUBLICATION-PROOF.md` links approval, release CI, registry integrity, clean lock/no-fallback, imports/smoke/monitoring/rollback. Common/release gates.\n## Review\nRelease ops/final product/security.\n## Rollback\nH8 pinned compatibility cohort; honor defaults or disable.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"`F8B-PUBLICATION-PROOF.md` links approval, release CI, registry integrity, clean lock/no-fallback, imports/smoke/monitoring/rollback. Common/release gates.","status":"open","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:44.408534991Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:32.773880607Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","packages","ready-for-human","release","seneca"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.25","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:44.408534991Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.25","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.24","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:50.375401708Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:186:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.26","title":"H4a conditional Human Intention: map non-default workspaceTypeId data if audit triggers","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Trigger/decision\nInactive unless F4a finds semantic non-default workspaceTypeId. Then stop F4a and provide anonymized counts/provenance/semantics and before-after mapping preserving membership/default/session/history/delete/provisioning/rollback. Owner approves graph amendment + migration Bead. Never silently coerce.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nIf activated, written decision names mapping/cohorts/dry run/validation/rollback/new node; add as F4a blocker. Gate mutates no data.\n## Rollback\nNo-op.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"If activated, written decision names mapping/cohorts/dry run/validation/rollback/new node; add as F4a blocker. Gate mutates no data.","status":"deferred","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:44.805117909Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:32.205979579Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","deferred","human-intention","migration","workspace-type"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.26","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:44.805117909Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.26","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.13","type":"related","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:50.549566999Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:188:{"id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.1","title":"909 G1 — freeze AgentGateway v0 contract and conformance","description":"## Background\nG1 is the first implementation slice after H0. It freezes the placement-independent `AgentGateway` v0 semantic contract, stable errors, server-only admission and request-ledger contracts, and a reusable conformance suite. It changes no production runtime behavior.\n\n## Changed paths\n- `packages/agent/src/shared/gateway/types.ts` (new file)\n- `packages/agent/src/shared/gateway/errors.ts` (new file)\n- `packages/agent/src/shared/gateway/events.ts` (new file)\n- `packages/agent/src/shared/gateway/__tests__/dtoDiscipline.test.ts` (new file)\n- `packages/agent/src/shared/index.ts`\n- Agent package export declarations in `packages/agent/package.json`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/types.ts` (new file)\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/testing/gatewayConformance.ts` (new file)\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/testing/__tests__/gatewayConformance.test.ts` (new file)\n\n## Technical approach\nDefine the complete addressed contract: verified and authorized scope types; Agent catalog and session references; keyset session pages; create, connect, read, rename, and delete inputs; prompt and follow-up commands; interrupt, stop, and queue-clear controls; typed receipts; snapshots; connections; Gateway lifecycle; JSON-safe event envelopes with one `seq`; and every stable v0 error.\n\nKeep `AuthorizedAgentScope` non-serializable and issuer-owned. The verifier must reject casts, spread copies, JSON round trips, capabilities from another issuer, stale membership, and revoked membership. Reverify every operation and every command on an open connection.\n\nDefine server-only `AgentGatewayEffect`, target, key, failure, record, admission, and `AgentRequestLedger` types with exact transitions: missing to pending admission; accepted admission to in flight; strong rejection before effect; legacy observed rejection from in flight; completion; and outcome unknown. The Level-B fake is process-lifetime only.\n\nThe DTO guard is structural and type-level. Do not implement recursive runtime event-leaf validation or immutable snapshot pagination. Those are v2 and Level-D responsibilities. Parameterize pagination conformance separately from replay level and specify owner-annotated Level-D skips.\n\n## Test plan\nThe throwaway in-memory fake must compile and run the reusable conformance suite. Cover scope provenance, current membership, stable error mapping, every valid and invalid ledger transition, same-request retry, conflicting digest, cross-scope and cross-target request IDs, command-state transitions, close-is-unsubscribe, monotonic sequence, bounded replay gap recovery, snapshot consistency, total session order, cursor tamper and binding denial, moved-row behavior, deleted-row behavior, and a valid cursor yielding an empty page. Assert that Level-D restart, durable-ledger, durable-activity, immutable-snapshot, and remote-wire cases are named and skipped with owner annotations.\n\n## Runnable proof recipe\nRun from repository root:\n1. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent typecheck`\n2. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/agent-host/testing/__tests__/gatewayConformance.test.ts`\n3. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent lint:invariants`\n4. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent build`\n5. `git diff --check`\n\nExpected result: every command exits zero, shared exports resolve, invariant checks find no `node:*` or `Buffer` use, and the conformance output names all deferred cases. Manual and E2E proof are not applicable because G1 changes no production behavior. Attach command results and the exact skip list to the current-head proof comment.\n\n## Rollback\nRevert the G1 pull request before AH0 starts. No data or wire migration exists.\n\n## Considerations\nDo not leak arbitrary legacy admission codes into the closed public Gateway error union. Do not confuse `PiChatSnapshot` wire status with the coarse session-list activity status. Do not add `hostId`, provider details, roots, Fastify, Pi SDK, or live objects to shared DTOs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nThe canonical closure criteria are in this bead's acceptance-criteria field and are mandatory.","acceptance_criteria":"The epic contains dated H0/A0 approval before this bead changes from deferred.\nAll shared gateway types and stable errors compile and export from `@hachej/boring-agent/shared`; server-only admission/ledger types remain under agent-host.\nAuthorizedAgentScope forgery, spread/JSON copy, cross-issuer use, and stale membership fail closed on every operation and open-connection command.\nThe exact effect/target/key/failure/ledger state machine compiles and passes all valid/invalid CAS transition tests against the in-memory Level-B fake.\nLevel B conformance passes; every durable/restart/snapshot-registry/activity case is explicitly Level D/v2-skipped with owner annotation.\nKeyset tests cover binding/tamper denial plus mutation behavior: moved rows may shift, deleted rows disappear, and a still-valid cursor may yield an empty page.\nNo recursive runtime event validator or immutable snapshot registry is implemented in G1.\nAll five proof commands exit 0 and the current-PR-head proof comment records outputs and named skips.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"ubuntu","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:30:57.565370268Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T06:36:16.982782954Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T06:36:16.982546511Z","close_reason":"Merged PR #915 into issue-909/agent-gateway-v0 at 621cd0f58; current-head proof comment records exact five green commands, 29 passed/6 owner-skipped conformance cases, clean independent review, rollback, and no waiver.","source_repo":"issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["contract","g1","issue-909"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:30:57.565370268Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:189:{"id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.2","title":"909 AH0 — build createAgentHost and EmbeddedAgentGateway","description":"## Background\nAH0 is the sequential foundation after G1. It consolidates the two Agent constructors and the Core hand-assembly seam behind one `buildAgentComposition()` and one awaited `createAgentHost()`, implements `EmbeddedAgentGateway`, preserves all compatibility surfaces, and establishes five reviewable checkpoints in one pull request.\n\n## Changed paths\n- `docs/issues/909/AH0-ASSEMBLY-AUDIT.md` (new file)\n- `packages/agent/src/server/createAgentApp.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/registerAgentRoutes.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/**` (new implementation and tests)\n- `packages/agent/src/server/http/routes/piChat.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/http/routes/__tests__/piChat.test.ts`\n- session, rename, and activity seams under `packages/agent/src/server/pi-chat/**`\n- app-owned plugin preflight under `packages/workspace/src/server/agentPlugins/**`\n- `packages/workspace/src/server/agentPlugins/__tests__/canonicalPluginId.test.ts` (new file)\n- Agent-owned runtime-mode adapter exports and the Workspace re-export shim\n\n## Checkpoint A: exhaustive assembly audit\nBefore implementation, commit `docs/issues/909/AH0-ASSEMBLY-AUDIT.md`. Inventory every option, hook, route, lifecycle edge, and ordering constraint in `CreateAgentAppOptions`, `RegisterAgentRoutesOptions`, and `packages/core/src/app/server/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.ts:840-1135`. Every row must map to Host, normalized resolver, compatibility wrapper, or app-side ownership and name a regression test. Zero rows may remain unclassified.\n\nProof A:\n`pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/__tests__/createAgentApp.test.ts src/server/__tests__/registerAgentRoutes.test.ts src/server/__tests__/registerAgentRoutes.lifecycle.test.ts`\n\n## Checkpoint B: single funnel and frozen composition\nImplement `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/buildAgentComposition.ts` (new file) as the only harness-to-bridge-to-chat-service-to-session-store-to-tools sequence. Implement awaited `createAgentHost()` with non-empty cloned fleet validation, duplicate and unsafe ID rejection, app-owned fleet compilation, one-to-one compiler-output validation, recursive freeze, stable host identity, lazy runtime bindings, pinned session runtime identity, one writer, and a canonical Environment lease.\n\nCanonical plugin ID validation runs app-side before descriptors or contributions are collected. `package.json#boring.id`, `definePlugin({id})`, and `defineServerPlugin({id})` must agree; omitted `boring.id` falls back to package name. Runtime identity changes for artifact digest, validated config, grants, placement, isolation, tool-contract digest, and provisioning generation. A grant-only change must preserve `provisioningFingerprint` and Environment sharing.\n\nProof B:\n`pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/agent-host/__tests__/createAgentHost.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/fleetCompiler.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/runtimeScopeIdentity.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/environmentLease.test.ts`\n\nAll four paths are new files created by this bead.\n\n## Checkpoint C: Embedded Gateway and honest Level B\nImplement `EmbeddedAgentGateway` over the shared composition with a process-lifetime in-memory request ledger, strong effect admission, the legacy at-most-once compatibility adapter, scope-bound keyset pagination, bounded replay, snapshot recovery, no-boot activity derivation, and deterministic rename. Rename appends `session_info` to every resolved wrapper and linked-native transcript through the existing append path under one writer lock. Newest durable entry wins by timestamp, then native over wrapper, then byte offset. No rename journal, cross-process lock protocol, durable request ledger, or durable activity checkpoint lands here.\n\nProof C:\n`pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/agent-host/testing/__tests__/embeddedGatewayConformance.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/requestLedger.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/renameSession.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/sessionIsolation.test.ts`\n\nAll four paths are new files created by this bead.\n\n## Checkpoint D: HTTP compatibility projection\nImplement the awaited Fastify projection and addressed routes. Rewrite `createAgentApp` and `registerAgentRoutes` as signature-compatible delegating wrappers. Preserve every legacy method, path, query, body, status, header, error body, heartbeat, NDJSON frame, attachment response, prompt, follow-up, queue-clear, interrupt, and stop behavior. Preserve explicit `sessionDir`, namespaced `sessionRoot`, and CLI `defaultSessionDir` branches without moving or copying transcripts. Add the in-process projected-tool conformance test proving `onUpdate` and `AbortSignal` survive schema projection.\n\nProof D:\n`pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/http/routes/__tests__/piChat.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/legacyTranscriptCompatibility.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/projectedToolConformance.test.ts src/server/__tests__/createAgentApp.test.ts src/server/__tests__/registerAgentRoutes.test.ts`\n\nThe two `src/server/agent-host/__tests__` paths are new files created by this bead; the other paths already exist.\n\n## Checkpoint E: adapter relocation and lifecycle\nMove `createSandboxRuntimeModeAdapter` and `sandboxRuntimeHostOperations` into Agent-owned server exports and keep Workspace re-export shims. Record the `BORING_AGENT_HOST_ID` consumer inventory without renaming it. Implement idempotent Gateway close, Host drain, and Host close; cancel unbounded subscriptions; bound finite effects by `shutdownGraceMs`; fence late callbacks; dispose bindings, Environment leases, and the mode adapter once.\n\nProof E:\n`pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/agent-host/__tests__/lifecycle.test.ts src/server/runtime/__tests__/runtimeBindingLifecycle.test.ts src/server/runtime/modes/__tests__/providerAdapter.test.ts`\n\n`src/server/agent-host/__tests__/lifecycle.test.ts` is a new file created by this bead; the runtime tests already exist.\n\n## Manual and E2E proof\nRun `pnpm --filter workspace-playground dev`. Through the local UI, list two Agents in each of two Workspace scopes, create and connect sessions under two storage scopes, send prompts as two subjects with actor-varying tools, stop one turn, reconnect from a bounded cursor, rename a legacy transcript, and confirm no root, tool, prompt, transcript, storage, or actor bleed. Terminate the process with an active event subscriber and a stuck injected effect; confirm shutdown returns within the configured grace period. Repeat the legacy transcript fixture with `BORING_AGENT_SESSION_ROOT` unset and set to a temporary root.\n\n## PR proof and rollback\nKeep checkpoints A through E as distinct commits in one AH0 pull request. The current-head proof comment must include every proof command, manual observation, changed path, and named Level-D skip. Rollback reverts the AH0 pull request; the pre-AH0 transcript fixture must remain readable at the same byte paths before and after rollback.\n\n## Considerations\nCore and Workspace retain membership, database and plugin discovery, bridge and UI routes, asset and backend management, and trusted storage mapping. The Host never imports Core or Workspace discovery. No pre-descope durability or remote-wire machinery belongs in AH0.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nThe canonical closure criteria are in this bead's acceptance-criteria field and are mandatory.","acceptance_criteria":"Checkpoint A commits a zero-unclassified assembly audit with a regression test for every row before implementation proceeds.\nCheckpoint B makes buildAgentComposition the sole construction sequence; awaited createAgentHost validates/freezes the full fleet before serving, performs canonical-ID preflight app-side before contribution collection, and consumes only validated IDs in the fleet compiler.\nThe PL1 fixture changes runtime identity for every artifact/config/grant/placement/tool-contract/provisioning input while grant-only changes preserve provisioningFingerprint and the shared Environment lease.\nCheckpoint C passes EmbeddedAgentGateway Level B with process-lifetime ack-loss/conflict/concurrent retry, legacy failure replay within process, single-writer isolation, deterministic no-journal rename, and derived no-phantom activity. Durable crash/restart machinery remains Level D-skipped.\nCheckpoint D preserves every legacy wire/transcript/prompt byte and all three session-layout branches; delegating wrappers retain signatures; F7 proves onUpdate and AbortSignal survive in-process schema projection.\nCheckpoint E relocates runtime adapters with Workspace shims, records the naming inventory without env rename, and passes bounded/fenced lifecycle tests.\nTwo Workspaces, two Agent types, two storage scopes, and two subjects prove no root/tool/transcript/prompt/actor bleed; compatible Agents share one Environment generation and incompatible fingerprints fail without mutation.\nAll checkpoint commands and manual steps have expected results and are attached to a current-head PR proof comment; rollback reads the same pre-AH0 transcript bytes.\nOne-machinery invariant test: both contribution kinds (workspace-activated and agent-spec-activated) resolve through the same plugin resolver, canonical-ID preflight, artifact record, and loading lifecycle; the test fails if a second resolver/loader path exists (grep-level: exactly one resolver entry module) and proves activation-site filtering selects contributions without duplicating loading.","notes":"2026-07-24 OWNER RESOLUTION: continue AH0 redesign in the existing bead; no replan authorized. All four self-review gaps are existing acceptance criteria: awaited createAgentHost funnel delegation (step 4/checkpoint D), no-boot listSessions, persisted runtimeScopeIdentity per plan §6.10, and legacy-at-most-once request-ledger mapping per §6.10. Preserved exact-five checkpoint branch was pushed first at 723f5555f7da18c2388e36af5e0dd4b50b5ef48c. Execute four fresh sequential subagents, one gap at a time, each proved with its owning checkpoint commands. Interactive UI matrix completes under checkpoint D golden-route/front-E2E proof.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"ubuntu","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:30:58.307483954Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T16:48:29.690935658Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T16:48:29.690734223Z","close_reason":"Merged PR #920 into issue-909/agent-gateway-v0 at 4c05fb28b; current-head proof comment records exact checkpoint, full-suite, browser, rollback, skip, and residual-risk evidence; fresh final review returned SHIP and CI is green after the unrelated UI Review rerun.","source_repo":"issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["agent-host","ah0","factory","issue-909"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.2","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:30:58.307483954Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.2","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:16.094258736Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:190:{"id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.3","title":"909 MIG-WS — align Workspace servers and front addressing","description":"## Background\nMIG-WS makes Workspace an explicit composition root after AH0. Workspace stops constructing Agent internals and stops importing provider-specific runtime implementation while preserving the existing browser experience and compatibility wire.\n\n## Changed paths\n- `packages/workspace/src/app/server/createWorkspaceAgentServer.ts`\n- `packages/workspace/src/server/createWorkspaceAgentServer.ts`\n- `packages/workspace/src/app/server/__tests__/createWorkspaceAgentServer.test.ts`\n- `packages/workspace/src/server/__tests__/createWorkspaceAgentServer.test.ts`\n- `packages/workspace/src/app/front/__tests__/WorkspaceAgentFront.test.tsx`\n- `packages/workspace/src/front/chrome/session-list/__tests__/SessionBrowser.test.tsx`\n- Workspace front Agent and session transport under `packages/workspace/src/app/front/**`\n- `apps/workspace-playground/**`\n- package import and invariant scans\n\n## Technical approach\nReplace direct `createAgentApp` and Agent-internal construction with exactly one Workspace composition root calling `createAgentHost()`. Inject its Gateway and route plugin into Workspace session and chat surfaces. Workspace continues to own plugin assets, reload, backends, UI bridge, authorization, storage selection, and browser fallback.\n\nThread `agentTypeId` additively through front transport, reducers, and session-list actions. Preserve all legacy routes, NDJSON framing and heartbeats, errors, attachments, default-Agent behavior, and existing browser expectations. Derive `AuthorizedAgentScope` only from current membership and trusted Workspace/storage mapping. Reject foreign or stale selectors before capability minting; absent selector uses the app-defined default.\n\n## Runnable proof recipe\nRun from repository root:\n1. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace typecheck`\n2. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace exec vitest run src/app/server/__tests__/createWorkspaceAgentServer.test.ts src/server/__tests__/createWorkspaceAgentServer.test.ts`\n3. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace exec vitest run src/app/front/__tests__/WorkspaceAgentFront.test.tsx src/front/chrome/session-list/__tests__/SessionBrowser.test.tsx`\n4. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace build && pnpm --filter workspace-playground test && pnpm --filter workspace-playground build`\n5. `pnpm audit:imports && pnpm lint:invariants && git diff --check`\n\nExpected result: every command exits zero and import scans find no value import from Bash, Sandbox, Agent server internals, `HarnessPiChatService`, or `PiSessionStore` in target paths.\n\nManual proof: run `pnpm --filter workspace-playground dev`; list Agents, create and connect an addressed session, prompt, follow up, interrupt, stop, clear the queue, reconnect, rename, and delete. Confirm the legacy default route performs the same flow and browser framing and errors are unchanged.\n\n## Rollback\nRevert the MIG-WS pull request to AH0's delegating wrapper composition. Do not move or copy transcripts and do not change browser routes.\n\n## Considerations\nOnly the Workspace composition root may call `createAgentHost()`. Do not expose `hostId`, provider details, roots, or plugin backend state to the browser.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nThe canonical closure criteria are in this bead's acceptance-criteria field and are mandatory.","acceptance_criteria":"Workspace target paths have zero value imports from boring-bash, boring-sandbox, HarnessPiChatService, PiSessionStore, or Agent server internals.\nExactly one Workspace composition root owns createAgentHost; session/chat routes consume the injected Gateway.\nLegacy front flows, NDJSON framing/heartbeats/errors, attachments, default behavior, and existing E2E expectations are unchanged.\nAddressed transport carries agentTypeId additively without hostId/provider/root leakage.\nForeign/stale storage selectors fail before capability minting and the absent-selector default remains app-defined.\nWorkspace-playground completes the one-process manual smoke and automated build/test.\nAll five proof command groups exit with expected results and the current-head PR proof comment records automated/manual/rollback evidence.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:30:59.031797557Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T18:53:48.734097901Z","source_repo":"issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["issue-909","migration","workspace"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:30:59.031797557Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:16.475168776Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:191:{"id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.4","title":"909 MIG-CORE — align Core production composition","description":"## Background\nMIG-CORE migrates the production composition path. Core currently hand-assembles Agent routes alongside membership, database stores, plugins, bridge and UI routes, request-aware tools, provisioning, and fallback behavior. This bead replaces only Agent construction and consumption while retaining all app-owned policy.\n\n## Changed paths\n- `packages/core/src/app/server/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.ts`\n- `packages/core/src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.test.ts`\n- `packages/core/src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.provisioning.test.ts`\n- `packages/core/src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.workspaceBridge.test.ts`\n- `packages/core/src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.storageScope.test.ts` (new file)\n- `packages/core/src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.effectAdmission.test.ts` (new file)\n- additive Agent factory option types only if the refreshed audit proves a missing normalized seam\n\n## Merge gate 1: refreshed production audit\nBefore changing production composition, revalidate `docs/issues/909/AH0-ASSEMBLY-AUDIT.md` against `packages/core/src/app/server/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.ts:840-1135`. Every Core option, route, hook, lifecycle edge, and ordering constraint must still have a disposition and regression test. Commit the refreshed zero-unclassified table before gate 2.\n\nProof gate 1:\n`pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-core exec vitest run src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.test.ts src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.provisioning.test.ts src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.workspaceBridge.test.ts`\n\n## Merge gate 2: production composition cutover\nKeep Core authorization, current membership checks, trusted storage mapping, database and plugin discovery, bridge and UI routes, request-aware filesystem bindings, prompt contributions, provisioning, remote-worker Environment mode, and front fallback app-side. Construct one Host with normalized callbacks, call `createAgentHost()` once, and await `app.register(host.registerRoutes(options))` at the audited order point. Remove Core's direct harness, Pi service, session store, and provider construction.\n\nProof gate 2:\n`pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-core exec vitest run src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.test.ts src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.provisioning.test.ts src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.workspaceBridge.test.ts src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.telemetry.test.ts src/app/server/__tests__/createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer.telemetry-smoke.test.ts`\n\n## Merge gate 3: authorization, admission, and production behavior\nUse strong `effectAdmission: AgentEffectAdmission` for create, rename, delete, prompt, follow-up, interrupt, stop, and queue clear. Keep inherited `admitEffect` only in the compatibility wrapper. Reject an unknown fleet, plugin, model, or config before serving. Reject revoked membership and foreign or stale storage selectors before scope minting. Exercise production multi-Agent, multi-storage, multi-subject, provisioning, plugin-route, bridge, telemetry, and front-fallback behavior.\n\nProof gate 3:\n1. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-core typecheck`\n2. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-core test`\n3. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/agent-host/__tests__/effectAdmission.test.ts`\n4. `pnpm audit:imports && pnpm lint:invariants && git diff --check`\n\n`packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/__tests__/effectAdmission.test.ts` is a new file created by AH0.\n\nManual production proof: run `pnpm --filter full-app dev`; authenticate two subjects, exercise two Agent types and two storage scopes, revoke one subject during an open connection, attempt a foreign storage selector, invoke a request-aware tool, and verify plugin routes, Workspace bridge, provisioning, telemetry, and front fallback remain functional.\n\n## Rollback\nRevert the Core composition commit to AH0's delegating compatibility wrapper. No transcript migration or public-wire change occurs. Preserve the gate-1 audit record for diagnosis.\n\n## Considerations\nDo not bypass the refreshed audit to meet a package boundary. Add a narrowly typed factory option if a missing normalized seam is proven. Core remains the owner of policy and trust; the Agent Host owns mechanism.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nThe canonical closure criteria are in this bead's acceptance-criteria field and are mandatory.","acceptance_criteria":"Gate 1 records a refreshed zero-unclassified Core audit before migration code.\nGate 2 makes Core call createAgentHost once and await registerRoutes at the audited order point; Core no longer hand-assembles Agent internals.\nApp-owned auth/membership/storage mapping, DB/plugin discovery/trust, bridge/UI/plugin routes, request-aware bindings, and front fallback remain Core-side.\nGate 3 uses strong effectAdmission for all eight effects; legacy admitEffect remains wrapper-only and source-compatible.\nUnknown fleet/plugin/model/config fails before serving; revoked membership and foreign/stale selectors fail before scope minting.\nActual production-path multi-Agent/storage/actor, provisioning, plugin-route, bridge, and fallback proofs pass.\nAll proof commands and manual Core E2E steps have expected results in a current-head PR proof comment; rollback is the single Core composition commit.","status":"in_progress","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"ubuntu","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:30:59.771419378Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T16:48:59.674597685Z","source_repo":"issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["core","issue-909","migration","production-path"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.4","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:30:59.771419378Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.4","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:16.855939857Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:192:{"id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.5","title":"909 MIG-CLI — align CLI composition and native session layout","description":"## Background\nMIG-CLI removes the CLI's Workspace runtime-adapter reach-through while preserving native Pi session layout and trusted-local authorization.\n\n## Changed paths\n- `packages/cli/src/server/modeApps.ts`\n- `packages/cli/src/server/__tests__/modeApps.agentHost.test.ts` (new file)\n- Agent runtime-adapter public exports consumed by CLI\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/__tests__/renameSession.test.ts` (new file created by AH0)\n- CLI package import scans\n\n## Technical approach\nCall `createAgentHost()` through Agent-package exports and remove Workspace adapter imports. Mint one fixed trusted-local scope that cannot sign arbitrary browser, Workspace, or storage input. Preserve all three existing transcript branches: explicit `sessionDir`, `sessionRoot/<sessionNamespace>`, and `defaultSessionDir(storageCwd ?? cwd, sessionRoot)`. Test with `BORING_AGENT_SESSION_ROOT` unset and set to a temporary fixture root.\n\nPreserve standalone Pi interoperability and the single-writer lease. Rename appends through the existing session-store path to every resolved wrapper and linked-native transcript. Authority order is timestamp, native over wrapper, then byte offset. Loads perform no repair writes; convergence is guaranteed by the next explicit rename. Do not add a journal or lock-file protocol.\n\n## Runnable proof recipe\n1. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli typecheck`\n2. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli exec vitest run src/server/__tests__/modeApps.agentHost.test.ts`\n3. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli test`\n4. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/agent-host/__tests__/renameSession.test.ts`\n5. `pnpm audit:imports && git diff --check`\n\nRun command 2 once with `BORING_AGENT_SESSION_ROOT` unset and once with `BORING_AGENT_SESSION_ROOT` set to an isolated temporary fixture directory. Expected result: all commands exit zero, both fixtures read the same expected transcript bytes, and the CLI has no Workspace runtime-adapter import.\n\n## Rollback\nRevert the CLI composition pull request. No transcript migration occurs, so all prior byte paths remain readable.\n\n## Considerations\nLevel B does not promise cross-restart receipt replay. CLI trusted-local authorization is not a browser capability issuer.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nThe canonical closure criteria are in this bead's acceptance-criteria field and are mandatory.","acceptance_criteria":"CLI calls createAgentHost through Agent exports and has no Workspace runtime-adapter reach-through.\nTrusted-local scope is fixed and cannot sign arbitrary browser/workspace/storage input.\nAll three transcript branches remain byte-identical with BORING_AGENT_SESSION_ROOT set and unset; rollback reads the same bytes.\nRename uses timestamp/native/offset authority, converges by the next explicit rename, performs no load repair, and introduces no journal/lock protocol.\nStandalone Pi interoperability and one-writer behavior pass.\nAll five proof groups and manual fixture steps have expected results in the current-head PR proof comment.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:00.463046936Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T18:53:48.764486151Z","source_repo":"issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["cli","issue-909","migration"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.5","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:00.463046936Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.5","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:17.318035932Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:196:{"id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.9","title":"909 follow-up — revive authored Agent catalog","description":"## Background\nThe authored-definition materializer and deployment digests exist without production callers. This follow-up reconnects them to configured Agent Host specs and the catalog while preserving the authored-data trust boundary.\n\n## Changed paths\n- `packages/agent/src/shared/agent-definition.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agentDefinition/materializeAgentDirectory.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agentDefinition/__tests__/materializeAgentDirectory.test.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agentDefinition/__tests__/materializeAgentDirectory.trustBoundary.test.ts`\n- Agent Host catalog and prompt composition under `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/**`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/http/routes/__tests__/systemPrompt.test.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/__tests__/catalogDefinition.test.ts` (new file)\n- a Boring-side MacroAnalyst prompt-compatibility fixture\n\n## Technical approach\nBack `ConfiguredAgentHostAgentSpec.definition` with deterministic `materializeAgentDirectory` output and content-addressed deployment digests. Populate `AgentSummary.definition` with version and digest. Artifact identity is content identity, not semver.\n\nAuthored source remains inert data: identity, label, version, and instructions only. It cannot activate executable behavior, packages, paths, providers, credentials, capabilities, or grants. The app-owned fleet compiler binds only validated IDs and allowlisted loaded capabilities.\n\nConsolidate the three MacroAnalyst prompt inputs onto one precedence order: harness base, authored instructions, Host static append, then dynamic contribution. Preserve the legacy sentinel byte-for-byte.\n\n## Runnable proof recipe\n1. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/agentDefinition/__tests__/materializeAgentDirectory.test.ts src/server/agentDefinition/__tests__/materializeAgentDirectory.trustBoundary.test.ts`\n2. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/http/routes/__tests__/systemPrompt.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/catalogDefinition.test.ts`\n3. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent typecheck && pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent build`\n4. `pnpm audit:imports && git diff --check`\n\nExpected result: all commands exit zero, hostile authored fields fail closed, configured prompts differ as expected, and the legacy golden is unchanged.\n\nManual proof: materialize two fixture directories with different instructions, list both through `AgentGateway`, inspect version and digest, execute one prompt per Agent, and verify the canonical precedence. Link any required external MacroAnalyst pull request by exact URL and commit SHA.\n\n## Rollback\nRevert catalog binding. Definitions return to optional summaries and the legacy prompt remains unchanged. No authored directory is deleted.\n\n## Considerations\nDo not expose installation, marketplace, health, provider, or Host routing state in `AgentSummary`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nThe canonical closure criteria are in this bead's acceptance-criteria field and are mandatory.","acceptance_criteria":"Configured definitions materialize deterministically and AgentSummary.definition exposes correct content version/digest.\nAuthored JSON cannot activate executable behavior, code, packages, paths, providers, credentials, or grants; fleet compiler binds only app-loaded allowlists.\nThe three Macro prompt paths are represented by one canonical precedence chain with a Boring-side fixture and any required external PR linked explicitly.\nDifferent authored instructions produce distinct expected prompts and the legacy sentinel golden remains byte-identical.\nAll four proof groups and manual catalog/prompt steps have expected results in the current-head PR proof comment; rollback leaves legacy prompt behavior intact.\nVocabulary conformance: catalog code/docs use the canonical ontology (Agent / agent plugin / workspace plugin; macro is an Agent, deck is an agent plugin, automation is a workspace plugin); no 'capability'/'vertical' nouns for these concepts and Hosts never appear as product nouns.\nPrompt fragments preserve structured provenance (fragment ID, source artifact digest, precedence phase) through resolution up to final rendering; the resolved prompt manifest is inspectable in the fixture before string rendering.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:03.242548359Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-23T20:35:55.971666394Z","source_repo":"issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["catalog","follow-up","issue-909"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:03.242548359Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.17","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-23T20:35:55.971023602Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:19.387123282Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:206:{"id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.1","title":"G1 prove live HTTP/WS authority and attachment","description":"## Fixed product contract\nImplement GitHub #912 only: /live start \"title\", /live stop, /live status; compact explicit consent; one statically composed singleton; one live session/microphone owner per workspace in one owning app process; stream-only audio to private pinned Kyutai/Moshi stt-1b-en_fr through an authenticated same-origin backend proxy; no audio retention; one timestamped non-diarized Markdown artifact read-only in the live UI; revision-safe projection at most once/second; browser socket close is terminal; only one upstream Kyutai restart; same originating chat stays usable and receives changed-only hidden reviews at +60s then +120s; exact NO_LIVE_RECOMMENDATION is suppressed. Flag remains off until final owner approval.\n\n## Non-goals\nNo MediaRecorder, chunks, upload, playback, pause/resume, browser reconnect, reload/crash recovery, diarization, transcript cards, modes, provider abstraction, generic audio/WebSocket/job/hidden-turn platform, distributed lease, dynamic provider mounting, query credentials, or old recording subsystem integration. Transcript text is untrusted. Stable errors, Workspace-only file access, and repository import invariants apply.\n\n## Scope\nCreate the smallest flag-off contract proof for a core/full-app-owned resolver shared by HTTP mutations and WebSocket upgrades. It must return authenticated principalId, workspaceId, chat-session authority, and resolved Workspace; reject client IDs/raw roots/local-only actor as production authority; reuse host CSRF policy for HTTP; require one canonical allowed Origin for upgrade; and prove a 256-bit hashed single-use pending-attachment capability delivered in the first strict binary message with a 15-second orphan deadline. Start/attachment capability binds principal/workspace/chat/live-session/connection; wrong scope, reuse, expiry, and same-principal competing tabs fail closed. No accepting audio route.\n\n## Repository seams\nInspect packages/core/src/app/server/{createCoreWorkspaceAgentServer,coreWorkspaceBridge}.ts and tests; packages/workspace/src/app/server/createWorkspaceAgentServer.ts only for explicit local-only development composition. Do not widen generic external-plugin auth APIs.\n\n## Acceptance/proof\nAPI-level HTTP+upgrade tests cover valid auth, absent auth, membership/session mismatch, spoofed workspace headers, missing/invalid CSRF, allowed and absent/null/malformed/multi-valued/hostile Origin, attachment redemption/reuse/theft/expiry, and deadline cleanup that revision-safely interrupts when possible and releases lease/lock. Record exact production symbols and commands on issue #912. Feature flag and audio acceptance remain off.\n\n## Status non-disclosure\nUnauthorized, non-member, cross-workspace, cross-session, non-owner, spoofed and capability-only status calls reveal no active path, title, session ID, lease, capability, or upstream detail; return only stable non-secret idle/authorization results after host authority checks.","acceptance_criteria":"Focused core/full-app HTTP+upgrade tests prove: (a) invalid/spoofed HTTP or upgrade authority, CSRF, Origin, and capability redemption fail before live-route Workspace operations or audio acceptance; (b) a valid pending-start expiry uses only its already resolved Workspace, revision-safely marks interrupted when expected bytes still match, revokes capability, and releases lease/lock. Cover membership/session mismatch, same-principal tab race, expiry/reuse, and redaction. Commands: pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-core test; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-core typecheck; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace test; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace typecheck; pnpm audit:imports; git diff --check. Record exact test paths/production symbols.","notes":"INCONCLUSIVE 2026-07-24: isolated worker exceeded its turn budget before an acceptance report/commit; harness removed the temporary worktree, so no proof was retained. Gate has not passed. Implementation remains stopped because G2-G4 independently failed. Evidence: docs/issues/912/feasibility/2026-07-24-gate-results.md","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:12.023305926Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.345221250Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.344847830Z","close_reason":"Original production feasibility investigation complete; outcome and blockers are recorded. Superseded by owner-approved local V0 plan.","source_repo":"issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["912","auth","feasibility","security","websocket"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:12.023305926Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:207:{"id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.2","title":"G2 prove private same-chat review publication","description":"## Fixed product contract\nImplement GitHub #912 only: /live start \"title\", /live stop, /live status; compact explicit consent; one statically composed singleton; one live session/microphone owner per workspace in one owning app process; stream-only audio to private pinned Kyutai/Moshi stt-1b-en_fr through an authenticated same-origin backend proxy; no audio retention; one timestamped non-diarized Markdown artifact read-only in the live UI; revision-safe projection at most once/second; browser socket close is terminal; only one upstream Kyutai restart; same originating chat stays usable and receives changed-only hidden reviews at +60s then +120s; exact NO_LIVE_RECOMMENDATION is suppressed. Flag remains off until final owner approval.\n\n## Non-goals\nNo MediaRecorder, chunks, upload, playback, pause/resume, browser reconnect, reload/crash recovery, diarization, transcript cards, modes, provider abstraction, generic audio/WebSocket/job/hidden-turn platform, distributed lease, dynamic provider mounting, query credentials, or old recording subsystem integration. Transcript text is untrusted. Stable errors, Workspace-only file access, and repository import invariants apply.\n\n## Scope\nAgainst the pinned Pi integration, prove a narrowly named same-session live-transcript review operation. Hidden trusted instruction gets one host-defined exact-path/expected-revision Workspace read capability and no shell/network/write/arbitrary-file/UI/other tools. User turns win; due reviews defer/coalesce. Buffer full assistant output before classification. Hidden instruction/path/tool call/tool result/transcript/sentinel may exist only in bounded in-flight memory and must not enter browser streams, Boring events/snapshots, native Pi entries, reload, compaction/next-turn context, logs, or telemetry. Only the byte-for-byte exact complete result NO_LIVE_RECOMMENDATION publishes nothing; prefixes, suffixes, and any whitespace-modified result publish as useful output; a complete useful result commits once as a normal assistant message in the immutable originating chat. Cancellation/error publishes no partial output.\n\n## Repository seams\npackages/agent/src/core/piChatSessionService.ts; server/pi-chat/PiAgentSessionAdapter.ts; server/harness/pi-coding-agent/{createHarness,sessions}.ts and adjacent tests. Do not expose a browser-generic hidden-turn command or use UI filtering/second agent/visible synthetic prompt as fallback.\n\n## Acceptance/proof\nTests inspect every persistence/publication surface above, ordering behind active user turns, coalescing, exact-path/revision denial, prompt-injection transcript, sentinel/near-match, cancellation, reload and future context. If pinned Pi cannot satisfy all semantics, stop and return ready-for-human; do not weaken.","acceptance_criteria":"Tests prove same-session ordering and coalescing; exact-path/revision restriction; hidden input/tool/transcript/sentinel absence from native/Boring/browser/reload/compaction/log surfaces; cancellation has no partial output; only byte-for-byte exact NO_LIVE_RECOMMENDATION suppresses, while leading/trailing whitespace and all near-matches publish once. Commands: pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent test; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent typecheck; pnpm audit:imports; git diff --check.","notes":"FAILED 2026-07-24: pinned Pi 0.80.7 has ordinary persisted/subscribed prompt/followUp only; no private same-session generation plus atomic useful-result-only publication primitive. Forbidden fallbacks were not implemented. Owner decision required. Evidence: docs/issues/912/feasibility/2026-07-24-gate-results.md","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:12.190568466Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.392809708Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.392506430Z","close_reason":"Original production feasibility investigation complete; outcome and blockers are recorded. Superseded by owner-approved local V0 plan.","source_repo":"issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["912","agent","feasibility","privacy","prompt-injection"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.2","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:12.190568466Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:209:{"id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.4","title":"G4 pin Kyutai CUDA protocol and non-retention","description":"## Fixed product contract\nImplement GitHub #912 only: /live start \"title\", /live stop, /live status; compact explicit consent; one statically composed singleton; one live session/microphone owner per workspace in one owning app process; stream-only audio to private pinned Kyutai/Moshi stt-1b-en_fr through an authenticated same-origin backend proxy; no audio retention; one timestamped non-diarized Markdown artifact read-only in the live UI; revision-safe projection at most once/second; browser socket close is terminal; only one upstream Kyutai restart; same originating chat stays usable and receives changed-only hidden reviews at +60s then +120s; exact NO_LIVE_RECOMMENDATION is suppressed. Flag remains off until final owner approval.\n\n## Non-goals\nNo MediaRecorder, chunks, upload, playback, pause/resume, browser reconnect, reload/crash recovery, diarization, transcript cards, modes, provider abstraction, generic audio/WebSocket/job/hidden-turn platform, distributed lease, dynamic provider mounting, query credentials, or old recording subsystem integration. Transcript text is untrusted. Stable errors, Workspace-only file access, and repository import invariants apply.\n\n## Scope\nPin the exact Kyutai/Moshi Rust server image digest/crate commit, stt-1b-en_fr model revision, CUDA/driver requirements, private WebSocket auth/handshake, MessagePack Audio/Marker and Ready/Word/EndWord/Step/Error schemas, 24kHz mono float PCM 1920-sample cadence, semantic pause meaning, timestamps, final drain, close behavior, and capacity for one stream. Commit digest-pinned fixtures/attestation and service config with request/body logging and dumps disabled, no writable audio sink, and controlled logs. Distinguish app non-persistence from operator service attestation.\n\n## State proof\nBrowser socket close is terminal. Only upstream Kyutai may restart once after one second while browser remains attached; downtime audio is dropped, not buffered/replayed; new provider epoch resets dedupe and receives a monotonic capture-clock offset; second failure interrupts.\n\n## Acceptance/proof\nScripted wire fixtures plus real CUDA smoke prove handshake/events/semantic pause/final drain/upstream restart/terminal browser close, exact pinned identity, GPU readiness, and service non-retention configuration. AudioWorklet bundling viability is attested. No mutable tag, public Moshi port, query credential, browser secret, or unsupported raw PCM assumption. Failed contract returns ready-for-human.","acceptance_criteria":"Commit digest-pinned Kyutai/Moshi stt-1b-en_fr wire fixtures and deployment attestation; prove one live stream on target CUDA, exact 24kHz/1920-sample framing, Word/EndWord/Step semantics, final drain, terminal browser close, one upstream-only restart/new epoch, and configured non-retention. Commands: pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-live-transcription test; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-live-transcription typecheck; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-live-transcription lint; BORING_LIVE_CUDA_SMOKE=1 pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-live-transcription smoke:cuda; git diff --check. Name the fixture/smoke files in proof.","notes":"KYUTAI FAILED 2026-07-24 for retention/protocol/image reasons. Owner approved a replacement-provider spike with anonymous diarization. WhisperLiveKit source contract passed, but target CUDA/French multi-speaker/container non-retention proof is blocked because this host has no NVIDIA runtime. Replacement spike: wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.10. Evidence: docs/issues/912/spikes/whisperlivekit/README.md","status":"closed","priority":0,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:12.606956008Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.437095232Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.436796963Z","close_reason":"Original production feasibility investigation complete; outcome and blockers are recorded. Superseded by owner-approved local V0 plan.","source_repo":"issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["912","cuda","feasibility","kyutai","privacy"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.4","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:12.606956008Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:210:{"id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.5","title":"V1 implement flag-off authority route unit","description":"## Fixed product contract\nImplement GitHub #912 only: /live start \"title\", /live stop, /live status; compact explicit consent; one statically composed singleton; one live session/microphone owner per workspace in one owning app process; stream-only audio to private pinned Kyutai/Moshi stt-1b-en_fr through an authenticated same-origin backend proxy; no audio retention; one timestamped non-diarized Markdown artifact read-only in the live UI; revision-safe projection at most once/second; browser socket close is terminal; only one upstream Kyutai restart; same originating chat stays usable and receives changed-only hidden reviews at +60s then +120s; exact NO_LIVE_RECOMMENDATION is suppressed. Flag remains off until final owner approval.\n\n## Non-goals\nNo MediaRecorder, chunks, upload, playback, pause/resume, browser reconnect, reload/crash recovery, diarization, transcript cards, modes, provider abstraction, generic audio/WebSocket/job/hidden-turn platform, distributed lease, dynamic provider mounting, query credentials, or old recording subsystem integration. Transcript text is untrusted. Stable errors, Workspace-only file access, and repository import invariants apply.\n\n## Scope\nUsing passed G1 evidence, implement the narrowly named internal live route factory and core/full-app resolver wiring, host CSRF/origin enforcement, pending-attachment capability/deadline lifecycle, stable LIVE_* errors, redaction, and tests. Standalone wiring is explicitly local-only. Route registration must reject/omit audio while BORING_LIVE_TRANSCRIPTS_ENABLED is off.\n\n## Acceptance/proof\nAll G1 authorization/CSRF/origin/capability tests remain green at the composed public seam. Flag-off app exposes no /live command/status strip and accepts no audio. No generic plugin auth API, raw root, client authority, query/subprotocol token, or secret log. Run focused core/workspace tests, typechecks, import audits and git diff --check; record outputs.\n\n## Status route privacy\nPreserve G1 negative status matrix at the composed route: unauthorized/non-owner/cross-scope callers receive no active transcript/path/session details and only stable non-secret results.","acceptance_criteria":"G1-G4 are all closed/proven first. Composed internal route tests preserve every G1 auth/CSRF/Origin/attachment guarantee while flag-off exposes no command/status and accepts no audio. No generic plugin auth API or secret logging. Commands: pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-core test; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-core typecheck; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace test; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace typecheck; pnpm audit:imports; git diff --check. Record exact changed/test files and outputs.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:12.988785362Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.723874007Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.723562615Z","close_reason":"Superseded before implementation by reviewed local CPU V0 slices; no product code from these units was started.","source_repo":"issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["912","auth","flag-off","implementation","websocket"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.5","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:12.988785362Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.5","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:14.442998724Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.5","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:11:41.676752720Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.5","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.3","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:11:42.010393294Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.5","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.4","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:11:42.353205994Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:211:{"id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.6","title":"V2 implement flag-off exact-path review unit","description":"## Fixed product contract\nImplement GitHub #912 only: /live start \"title\", /live stop, /live status; compact explicit consent; one statically composed singleton; one live session/microphone owner per workspace in one owning app process; stream-only audio to private pinned Kyutai/Moshi stt-1b-en_fr through an authenticated same-origin backend proxy; no audio retention; one timestamped non-diarized Markdown artifact read-only in the live UI; revision-safe projection at most once/second; browser socket close is terminal; only one upstream Kyutai restart; same originating chat stays usable and receives changed-only hidden reviews at +60s then +120s; exact NO_LIVE_RECOMMENDATION is suppressed. Flag remains off until final owner approval.\n\n## Non-goals\nNo MediaRecorder, chunks, upload, playback, pause/resume, browser reconnect, reload/crash recovery, diarization, transcript cards, modes, provider abstraction, generic audio/WebSocket/job/hidden-turn platform, distributed lease, dynamic provider mounting, query credentials, or old recording subsystem integration. Transcript text is untrusted. Stable errors, Workspace-only file access, and repository import invariants apply.\n\n## Scope\nUsing passed G2 semantics and V1 authority types where Workspace access is needed, implement the narrowly named same-session exact-path/expected-revision review operation, atomic same-session ordering/publication, bounded complete-response buffering, exact sentinel suppression, and one useful assistant-message publication. Keep all hidden material out of native/Boring/browser/log/reload/compaction surfaces. No public browser endpoint and no generic hidden-turn platform.\n\n## Acceptance/proof\nG2 full persistence/publication matrix passes, including active-user priority, cancellation, prompt injection, sentinel near-match, reload and future context. Flag remains off and no live route accepts audio. Run focused agent tests/typecheck plus applicable audits and git diff --check; record outputs.","acceptance_criteria":"G2 persistence/publication matrix remains exact: invocation behind already-admitted user work, exact-path/revision denial, hostile transcript, byte-exact sentinel/whitespace near-match, cancellation, reload and future context. V2 does not implement timers, changed-only eligibility, deferral/coalescing, or review flushes; V5 owns scheduling. Flag remains off; no public endpoint. Commands: pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent test; pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent typecheck; pnpm audit:imports; git diff --check. Record exact changed/test files and outputs.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:13.175676353Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.804437518Z","closed_at":"2026-07-24T07:14:04.804128445Z","close_reason":"Superseded before implementation by reviewed local CPU V0 slices; no product code from these units was started.","source_repo":"issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-912-minimal-live-transcript","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["912","agent","flag-off","implementation","privacy"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:13.175676353Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:07:14.661978204Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-gh912-live-transcript-8r4g.5","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-23T22:0