origin/main:docs/issues/391/runtime-refactor/architecture/00-global-isa.md:59:- **PLUGIN-extensible host product**: both the workspace UI and the agents inside it are extensible by third parties — internally and externally — over real APIs (`definePlugin`/`defineServerPlugin`, `/api/v1/plugins/:pluginId/*`, the `boring-ui-plugin` CLI). eve/Flue extend *your own* agent; boring's plugin layer lets others extend the *host product* without forking it. See [`08-pluggable-agent-surfaces.md`](08-pluggable-agent-surfaces.md) "Plugin-extensibility" (with honest caveats: external plugins are trusted local code, hosted-iframe is future, `full-app` ships `externalPlugins:false`).
