origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:84:{"id":"wt-391-forward-c0u.3","title":"A1.2: trusted tool allowlists and collision-safe merge","description":"Extend materializeAgentDirectory() as the sole tool catalog resolver using a trusted per-agent ReadonlyMap allowlist. Resolve refs once in declaration order. Strict validator covers safe name, nonempty description, non-array schema object, valid readiness requirements, execute function. Add mergeTools collisionPolicy last-wins|error; preserve last-wins default and use error for authored/dev across standard/authored/plugin tools. Never dynamic-import authored modules.\n\n## Rollback\nRevert catalog resolution/strict validator/collision option; compatibility merge remains prior last-wins behavior; no persisted state.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nRef-free/valid allowlist pass; absent catalog/ref, invalid name/description/schema/readiness/execute, duplicate output and standard/authored/plugin collisions fail exact frozen codes; last-wins compatibility tests unchanged; error fails before runtime; outputs frozen; import spy proves no authored tool module load. Exact commands: `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent build`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent typecheck`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent test`; `pnpm lint:invariants`; `pnpm check:golden-path`; `git diff --check`. Record output/rollback/residual risks; Sol-high security review CLEAN.","acceptance_criteria":"Ref-free/valid allowlist pass; absent catalog/ref, invalid name/description/schema/readiness/execute, duplicate output and standard/authored/plugin collisions fail exact frozen codes; last-wins compatibility tests unchanged; error fails before runtime; outputs frozen; import spy proves no authored tool module load. Exact commands: `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent build`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent typecheck`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent test`; `pnpm lint:invariants`; `pnpm check:golden-path`; `git diff --check`. Record output/rollback/residual risks; Sol-high security review CLEAN.","notes":"Historical only after merged PR #846 (085836f53). Do not dispatch. Replacement graph: wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. #814 remains corrective migration input; #816/#817/Seneca #16 architecture is superseded.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","estimated_minutes":420,"created_at":"2026-07-18T08:56:59.311345387Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-20T13:08:38.761115711Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T13:08:38.760802273Z","close_reason":"Superseded by merged PR #846 and replacement graph wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9; preserve branch/PR evidence only.","source_repo":"issue-391-plan-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-391-plan-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","a1","agent","historical","security","superseded","tools"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-c0u.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-c0u","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-18T08:56:59.311345387Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-c0u.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-c0u.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-18T08:57:00.540219244Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:85:{"id":"wt-391-forward-c0u.4","title":"A1.3: boring-ui agent validate CLI","description":"Add `boring-ui agent validate <dir>`. Human output reports ID/version/label/instructions byte length/declared refs without content/paths. JSON success is {schemaVersion:1,ok:true,agent:{agentTypeId,version,label?,instructions:{present:true,byteLength},refs:{tools,capabilities,skills,mcpServers}}}; JSON failure is AgentCliErrorV1. Directory validation reports refs but never claims runtime resolution or deployment provenance.\n\n## Rollback\nRemove the additive `agent validate` branch/help/DTO; existing CLI commands and authored directories remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nSubprocess tests cover valid human/JSON, malformed/schema/missing/traversal/symlink/UTF8, invalid ID, refs reporting, exact envelopes/codes/fields/exits and redaction; existing help/commands green. Exact commands: `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent build`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent test`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli build`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli typecheck`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli test`; `pnpm lint:invariants`; `pnpm check:golden-path`; `git diff --check`. Record output/rollback/residual risks; Sol-high spec/security review CLEAN.","acceptance_criteria":"Subprocess tests cover valid human/JSON, malformed/schema/missing/traversal/symlink/UTF8, invalid ID, refs reporting, exact envelopes/codes/fields/exits and redaction; existing help/commands green. Exact commands: `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent build`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent test`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli build`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli typecheck`; `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli test`; `pnpm lint:invariants`; `pnpm check:golden-path`; `git diff --check`. Record output/rollback/residual risks; Sol-high spec/security review CLEAN.","notes":"Historical only after merged PR #846 (085836f53). Do not dispatch. Replacement graph: wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. #814 remains corrective migration input; #816/#817/Seneca #16 architecture is superseded.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","estimated_minutes":300,"created_at":"2026-07-18T08:56:59.558492360Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-20T13:08:38.128488654Z","closed_at":"2026-07-18T18:44:32.389349226Z","close_reason":"Implemented and merged via PR #815 at 7a21d3580; GPT-5.5/Sol loop final APPROVE/CLEAN.","source_repo":"issue-391-plan-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-391-plan-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","a1","authoring","cli","historical","superseded"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-c0u.4","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-c0u","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-18T08:56:59.558492360Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-c0u.4","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-c0u.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-18T08:57:00.664770464Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:102:{"id":"wt-391-forward-6gd.1","title":"SBX1.1: bind static remote-worker protocol + placement to landed SandboxProviderV1","description":"SBX1.1 — Delivers: Gate-C re-inventory; shared strict protocol schemas; static fleet config/bucket resolver; per-box short-lived capability auth including bounded SSE lifetime; V1 client/provider pair; stable errors; the named H5 `sandboxId <-> authorized workspaceId` tenant-binding invariant with authenticated create binding receipt; and the H3 seam replacing heuristic `withRuntimeEnvContributions()` plaintext merging with purpose-typed per-workspace secret references. Decision 27 model BYOK stays at the landed #820 host Pi request seam and is rejected by remote-worker/Sandbox exec; only non-model invocation-secret references may reach the worker stdin envelope. Extend #820 owner-only credential lifecycle with an explicit disabled/revoked tombstone that suppresses instance fallback, plus upstream-revocation receipt/state; clear/absence retains Decision 27 fallback semantics.\nBlocked by (gates, captured as prerequisites not bead edges so this is the ready/dispatchable head of the chain): Gates A-D and the tracker transaction; completed #808 Phase 1-3 swap/artifact proof; merged #820 16f.2 host-side per-request credential seam.\nProof/exit: Sandbox/Core/Agent focused build/typecheck/test/invariants; strict config, missing-workspace, per-box-token, capability-expiry, and SSE-expiry/invalidation negatives; pair lifecycle/idempotency/expiry/dispose/error tests; two-workspace x two-sandbox cross-product rejection on fs/events/exec/renew/delete before adapters (the tested tenant-binding invariant); authenticated-receipt/swapped-create-response rejection; Decision 27 rotation visible at the next host model request; owner-only emergency disable creates a durable tombstone, suppresses fallback immediately, best-effort aborts the active request, and requires upstream revocation receipt/state before resolved; clear/absence still uses the explicit Decision 27 fallback; retained Sandbox-exec no-model-key proof; purpose/model/cross-workspace reference negatives; non-model stdin-envelope proof; Agent value-import invariant. 6gd.1 does not pass without every H3 and H5 gate.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-20T09:06:10.596851043Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-22T04:32:56.993735808Z","closed_at":"2026-07-22T04:32:56.993569044Z","close_reason":"SBX1.1 merged as #855 (1a9d5b007)","source_repo":"sbx1-activation","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/sbx1-activation","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","808"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-6gd.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-6gd","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T09:06:10.596851043Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:134:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","title":"R4: declarative authored-source correction and validate CLI","description":"## Context\nCorrect #814's unused published `0.1.90` authored catalog/tool semantics in one owner-approved, separately reviewed follow-up without rewriting history. Authored data becomes identity, safe metadata, and instructions only.\n\n## Scope\n- Simplify source/materialization, remove the unused published catalog contract, migrate repository callers/tests atomically, simplify validate, and prove packed consumption. No compatibility window or dedicated `0.2.0` boundary.\n\n## Constraints\n- May start after R0 only when no active R1-R3 Agent-package writer overlaps.\n- R0 found the public `0.1.90` surface; the owner confirmed no consumers and closed R4.0 with the corrective-follow-up strategy.\n\n## Proof\n- All R4 children and packed Agent/CLI proof pass.\n\n## Success Criteria\nNo authored executable selector remains and validation covers only declarative source.","acceptance_criteria":"No authored executable selector remains and validation covers only declarative source.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.678624166Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:01.625691894Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T21:18:20.342601217Z","close_reason":"R4 complete in one corrective follow-up: declarative authored source and validate CLI with no catalog runtime semantics; full Agent tests, focused CLI tests, builds, invariants, and packed consumer proof pass.","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","authoring","cli","decision-28-retained-evidence","decision-resolved","r4"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.678624166Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:135:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.1","title":"R4.1: simplify frozen authored source and remove catalog runtime semantics","description":"## Context\nThe authored source loader remains useful, but tools/skills/MCP/package/model/runtime policy belong to trusted host plugins and configuration.\n\n## Scope\n- Keep definitionId, schema version, label, description, and bounded instructions only.\n- Require host agentTypeId exactly equals source definitionId; aliases are forbidden.\n- Preserve contained import-free reads, UTF-8/size/count/path/symlink protections, deterministic frozen/redacted output, and no sibling executable import.\n- Reject non-empty legacy capability/tool/skill/MCP references with stable migration errors.\n- In one corrective PR, remove `AuthoredAgentToolCatalog`, `MaterializeAgentDirectoryInput.toolCatalog`, materialized `tools`/`declaredToolRefs`, authored capability/tool/skill/MCP ref fields, and catalog-only error paths; migrate repository callers/tests atomically.\n- Keep `materializeAgentDirectory` and `compileAgentDirectory` as simplified declarative operations; preserve unrelated compiler/digest/deployment exports and `AUTHORED_AGENT_TOOL_COLLISION` while normal composition uses it.\n\n## Constraints\n- Authored input never selects executable path/package/credential/command/model/plugin or runtime policy.\n- No forced rewrite of reviewed history.\n- R4.0 is closed: no compatibility window or dedicated `0.2.0` boundary; rollback is a normal revert before I0 publication.\n\n## Proof\n- Bounds/path/symlink/UTF-8/ID/legacy-ref matrix, executable sentinel, freeze/redaction, and source ID mismatch tests.\n- Package export/typecheck proof.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nMaterialized source is declarative-only and unsupported executable metadata cannot affect composition. The implementation matches the approved corrective scope and removes no HTTP/product endpoint or unrelated public export.","acceptance_criteria":"Materialized source is declarative-only and unsupported executable metadata cannot affect composition. The implementation matches the approved R4.0 public-API migration and target version.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","assignee":"ubuntu","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.940953514Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:01.605865646Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T21:18:19.826666072Z","close_reason":"Implemented declarative-only authored source: removed catalog/tool-selector contracts, bounded race-checked no-symlink reads, safe metadata, frozen output, migration errors, tests, docs, and packed export proof.","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","agent","authoring","decision-28-retained-evidence","r4"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:07:40.940953514Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.1","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.3","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:50:21.933418626Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:157:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.3","title":"R4.0 gate: approve migration for published authored APIs","description":"## Context\nR0 proved that the #813-#815 authored APIs are not unpublished implementation details: `@hachej/boring-agent@0.1.90` publicly exports `materializeAgentDirectory`, `MaterializedAgentSourceV1`, `AuthoredAgentToolCatalog`, and catalog-related errors, while `@hachej/boring-ui-cli@0.1.90` ships `agent validate` and its schema-v1 output. R4 cannot remove or silently repurpose those contracts without an explicit release/migration decision.\n\n## Scope\n- Choose and document the compatibility strategy for the published 0.1.90 surface: coordinated breaking 0.2 release, deprecation/compatibility window plus a new declarative API, or another explicitly versioned migration.\n- Decide treatment of `tools`, `declaredToolRefs`, `toolCatalog`, catalog error codes, old definition ref arrays, and validate JSON/human fields.\n- Specify consumer migration for registry users, repository callers, golden-path timing, and superseded Seneca #16.\n- Mark every adjacent public compiler, definition, digest, validation, and deployment export listed in `R0-AUDIT.md` as preserve unchanged or define its versioned migration; preserve or separately migrate `AUTHORED_AGENT_TOOL_COLLISION` for the live normal tool composer.\n- Set the minimum rollback floor and whether I0 may publish the chosen break.\n- Update R4.1/R4.2 acceptance and docs before implementation.\n\n## Constraints\n- No direct R4 removal or semantic repurposing before this gate closes.\n- Stable errors/fields remain stable unless the approved version boundary and migration notes say otherwise.\n- The active runtime still must end with declarative authored identity/metadata/instructions only; compatibility must not reintroduce authored executable authority.\n\n## Proof\n- Registry declarations and integrity for Agent/CLI 0.1.90.\n- Public export/CLI field matrix from the R0 audit.\n- Written owner decision with target version, migration examples, package cohort, and rollback floor.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nOwner approves one explicit semver/migration strategy for every published authored surface, and R4.1/R4.2 are updated so implementation cannot silently break or preserve the wrong contract.\n\n## Owner decision — 2026-07-20\n- Confirmed: there are no consumers of the superseded authored catalog/materializer/validate surface.\n- Implement one separately reviewed corrective R4 follow-up PR; do not create a compatibility window or a dedicated `0.2.0` boundary.\n- Remove catalog/tool-selector authority and simplify validate; migrate all repository callers/tests atomically in that PR.\n- Preserve unrelated compiler/digest/deployment exports and preserve `AUTHORED_AGENT_TOOL_COLLISION` while normal tool composition uses it. No HTTP or product endpoint is removed.\n- Keep #816/#817 and Seneca #16 superseded; do not merge them as compatibility.\n- Rollback floor: revert the corrective PR before I0 publication. I0 still chooses and human-approves the later joint package cohort.\n","acceptance_criteria":"Owner approves one explicit semver/migration strategy for every published authored surface, and R4.1/R4.2 are updated so implementation cannot silently break or preserve the wrong contract.","notes":"Superseded/non-dispatchable under Decision 28. Preserve as historical planning evidence only. Current implementation authority is the Decision-28 F-series graph under wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9. Closed R0/R4 proof remains reusable where explicitly cited.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:50:21.269805096Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:13:01.649393101Z","closed_at":"2026-07-20T19:46:58.165031036Z","close_reason":"Owner approved one corrective R4 follow-up: no consumers, no compatibility window or dedicated 0.2.0 boundary; atomic repository migration; preserve unrelated exports/product APIs.","source_repo":"391-a1-beads-v2","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-a1-beads-v2","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","decision-28-retained-evidence","decision-recorded","r4"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.1","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:50:21.636503637Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6.3","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-20T13:50:21.269805096Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:166:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","title":"F0b: refresh current-main consumer, provider, publication, and migration inventory","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nRefresh retained R0 on merged F0a. Inventory every live read/write/edit/list/stat/mkdir/delete/move/find/grep/watch/exec consumer; provisioning/path/plugin/UI/CLI surface; package export/peer/registry/pack consumer; composition root; provider mechanic; session store; current-main #844 row/API behavior; #845 salvage. Distinguish current main from unmerged branches. Ground each fact in file/symbol or reproducible package evidence and assign F1-F8b owner.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n`F0B-INVENTORY.md/.json` are complete and machine-readable with zero unowned path; package/tarball facts reproduce; changed links/authority and diff checks pass.\n## Review\nCode-grounding and package architecture.\n## Rollback\nEvidence-only no-op; supersede with newer dated inventory.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"`F0B-INVENTORY.md/.json` are complete and machine-readable with zero unowned path; package/tarball facts reproduce; changed links/authority and diff checks pass.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:36.814449238Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:33.047836014Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["391","805","architecture","audit"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:36.814449238Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.1","type":"related","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:50.803494418Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.1.6","type":"related","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:50.993095952Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.6","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.5","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:45.186817659Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:169:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.9","title":"F2a: neutralize Sandbox backend contract and ratify provider enforcement","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nReplace final Agent-owned Workspace/Sandbox provider boundary with neutral backend handle for provisioning, canonical storage, exec, physical bindings, health/invalidation, persistence/cleanup; retain old exports during expansion. Ratify direct/bwrap/Vercel source of truth, locality, ops, physical binding/network, durability/watch/eligibility from code/tests. Every requirement is physical/advisory/unsupported. Hosted requires physical and fails stable unsupported when absent; direct/advisory is trusted-local unrestricted only. Remote staging may seed but never hide sync.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nProvider matrix + hostile tests prove actual mechanics, neutral imports, Vercel canonical-data ruling, direct/bwrap negatives and hosted network fail-closed. Sandbox test/typecheck/build + common gates; `F2A-PROVIDER-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nProvider, thermo, security.\n## Rollback\nOld exports/selection stay; no canonical data mutation.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Provider matrix + hostile tests prove actual mechanics, neutral imports, Vercel canonical-data ruling, direct/bwrap negatives and hosted network fail-closed. Sandbox test/typecheck/build + common gates; `F2A-PROVIDER-PROOF.md`.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:38.100511792Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:32.360613242Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","boring-sandbox","providers","security-review-required"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:38.100511792Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:45.847503451Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:172:{"id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","title":"F3a: add dedicated AgentApplication entrypoint and static fleet validator","description":"## Decision-28 invariants\n- One deployment-static validated AgentApplication fleet; no DB registry/controller/active pointer. Every fleet Agent is available to every authorized Workspace in v1; no per-Workspace allowlist. Agent identity is trusted deployment/CLI configuration; authored directories remain identity, bounded metadata, version and instructions only.\n- Ordinary Workspace owns persisted default, sessions, governance and orchestration. Web membership or CLI trusted-local policy authorizes every operation. Signup hostname only initializes a new Workspace default; it never authorizes, filters, selects existing Workspaces, or mutates a persisted default.\n- Core/web and CLI are independent Workspace consumers and never boot/route through one another.\n- `boring-bash` owns transport-neutral governed file/search/watch/exec Environment operations and coherence; `boring-sandbox` owns Agent/Workspace-neutral physical backends. All surfaces use one canonical filesystem; no copy/sync.\n- Reusable backend identity, invocation view, one-exec shell grants, and opaque model capability stay separate. Unsupported hosted physical enforcement fails closed.\n- AgentApplications are service-shaped but in-process v1. No public non-default selector, remote transport/discovery, distributed tasks, or contracted-agent policy.\n- Preserve authored-source safety, history/delete/ownership and lifecycle fencing. Stable errors. No file deletion without explicit written approval.\n\n## Scope\nPublish server-neutral `@hachej/boring-agent/application` with AgentApplication.invoke, immutable identity/version, invocation/session/model/Environment context, result/factory. No Fastify/UI/Core/CLI/Workspace implementation/provider values or front import. Workspace server owns and validates the frozen fleet grammar while importing the Agent application API: unique exact agentTypeId==definitionId, application default, trusted source/plugin-role references, no authored executable catalogs, no eager Workspace/App/Environment/model/backend. Host and CLI adapters compile to that one Workspace validator; Agent does not own a second fleet registry. Add ModelCapabilityIssuer port/fakes and opaque per-call model capability; hosted issuer F5a, CLI F6.\n## Acceptance Criteria\nTests cover invalid/duplicate IDs, missing default/ref/role, freeze/copy, eager negatives, pack/import direction and no credential capture. Agent test/typecheck/build + clean tarball + common; `F3A-APPLICATION-PROOF.md`.\n## Review\nAgent API/package layering.\n## Rollback\nAdditive entrypoint unused until cutover.\n## Common execution rule\nRun focused tests plus applicable `pnpm audit:imports`, `pnpm lint:invariants`, `pnpm check:golden-path`, and `git diff --check`. Record commands/exits/files/artifacts in the named proof. Use an isolated `.worktrees/` branch and keep the Bead `in_progress` until its implementation PR merges.","acceptance_criteria":"Tests cover invalid/duplicate IDs, missing default/ref/role, freeze/copy, eager negatives, pack/import direction and no credential capture. Agent test/typecheck/build + clean tarball + common; `F3A-APPLICATION-PROOF.md`. Workspace owns the sole fleet validator; Agent exposes only the application API and CLI does not embed another validator.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:39.204171791Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-21T21:25:31.517081616Z","source_repo":"391-agent-fleet-realignment","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/391-agent-fleet-realignment","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["805","agent","agent-application","fleet","package-api"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:39.204171791Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.12","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-step1a-current-xn9.8","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-21T21:17:46.526117725Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:.beads/issues.jsonl:196:{"id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.9","title":"909 follow-up — revive authored Agent catalog","description":"## Background\nThe authored-definition materializer and deployment digests exist without production callers. This follow-up reconnects them to configured Agent Host specs and the catalog while preserving the authored-data trust boundary.\n\n## Changed paths\n- `packages/agent/src/shared/agent-definition.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agentDefinition/materializeAgentDirectory.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agentDefinition/__tests__/materializeAgentDirectory.test.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agentDefinition/__tests__/materializeAgentDirectory.trustBoundary.test.ts`\n- Agent Host catalog and prompt composition under `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/**`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/http/routes/__tests__/systemPrompt.test.ts`\n- `packages/agent/src/server/agent-host/__tests__/catalogDefinition.test.ts` (new file)\n- a Boring-side MacroAnalyst prompt-compatibility fixture\n\n## Technical approach\nBack `ConfiguredAgentHostAgentSpec.definition` with deterministic `materializeAgentDirectory` output and content-addressed deployment digests. Populate `AgentSummary.definition` with version and digest. Artifact identity is content identity, not semver.\n\nAuthored source remains inert data: identity, label, version, and instructions only. It cannot activate executable behavior, packages, paths, providers, credentials, capabilities, or grants. The app-owned fleet compiler binds only validated IDs and allowlisted loaded capabilities.\n\nConsolidate the three MacroAnalyst prompt inputs onto one precedence order: harness base, authored instructions, Host static append, then dynamic contribution. Preserve the legacy sentinel byte-for-byte.\n\n## Runnable proof recipe\n1. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/agentDefinition/__tests__/materializeAgentDirectory.test.ts src/server/agentDefinition/__tests__/materializeAgentDirectory.trustBoundary.test.ts`\n2. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/http/routes/__tests__/systemPrompt.test.ts src/server/agent-host/__tests__/catalogDefinition.test.ts`\n3. `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent typecheck && pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent build`\n4. `pnpm audit:imports && git diff --check`\n\nExpected result: all commands exit zero, hostile authored fields fail closed, configured prompts differ as expected, and the legacy golden is unchanged.\n\nManual proof: materialize two fixture directories with different instructions, list both through `AgentGateway`, inspect version and digest, execute one prompt per Agent, and verify the canonical precedence. Link any required external MacroAnalyst pull request by exact URL and commit SHA.\n\n## Rollback\nRevert catalog binding. Definitions return to optional summaries and the legacy prompt remains unchanged. No authored directory is deleted.\n\n## Considerations\nDo not expose installation, marketplace, health, provider, or Host routing state in `AgentSummary`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nThe canonical closure criteria are in this bead's acceptance-criteria field and are mandatory.","acceptance_criteria":"Configured definitions materialize deterministically and AgentSummary.definition exposes correct content version/digest.\nAuthored JSON cannot activate executable behavior, code, packages, paths, providers, credentials, or grants; fleet compiler binds only app-loaded allowlists.\nThe three Macro prompt paths are represented by one canonical precedence chain with a Boring-side fixture and any required external PR linked explicitly.\nDifferent authored instructions produce distinct expected prompts and the legacy sentinel golden remains byte-identical.\nAll four proof groups and manual catalog/prompt steps have expected results in the current-head PR proof comment; rollback leaves legacy prompt behavior intact.\nVocabulary conformance: catalog code/docs use the canonical ontology (Agent / agent plugin / workspace plugin; macro is an Agent, deck is an agent plugin, automation is a workspace plugin); no 'capability'/'vertical' nouns for these concepts and Hosts never appear as product nouns.\nPrompt fragments preserve structured provenance (fragment ID, source artifact digest, precedence phase) through resolution up to final rendering; the resolved prompt manifest is inspectable in the fixture before string rendering.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:03.242548359Z","created_by":"ubuntu","updated_at":"2026-07-23T20:35:55.971666394Z","source_repo":"issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","source_repo_path":"/home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/issue-909-agent-gateway-v0","compaction_level":0,"original_size":0,"labels":["catalog","follow-up","issue-909"],"dependencies":[{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:03.242548359Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.17","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-23T20:35:55.971023602Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""},{"issue_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.9","depends_on_id":"wt-391-forward-0jpy.2","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-07-22T21:31:19.387123282Z","created_by":"ubuntu","metadata":"{}","thread_id":""}]}
origin/main:docs/DECISIONS.md:404:> identity, and full-app compatibility. Workspace now orchestrates a static fleet
origin/main:docs/DECISIONS.md:430:| **What** | #391 ships in product-led steps. **Step 1A:** exact trusted domain → persisted `workspaceTypeId` → authenticated membership-authorized Workspace → Workspace-selected default agent. Core owns authentication, membership, Workspace persistence, and typed list/select/create; it does not load or compose agents. Workspace owns deployment-static `defaultAgentTypeId` + `allowedAgentTypeIds`, one shared WorkspaceRuntime/Workspace/Sandbox, effective provisioning-plugin union, and a lazy actor-neutral singleton per `(workspaceId, agentTypeId)`. Agent loads/executes one requested type against that supplied runtime. The backend proves two allowed types share exact Workspace/Sandbox identity now, while public human ingress starts new sessions with only the default and accepts no arbitrary agent selector. Existing hosts normalize through the same orchestrator as `default → primary`. Authored agent data is declarative identity/safe metadata/instructions only; trusted host plugins own executable behavior. **Step 1B:** authenticated external MCP reaches the same authorized Workspace and server-selected default. **Step 2:** activate Workspace-local native collaboration after a `pi-subagents` executor/backend can share WorkspaceRuntime; human selector/switch/fork remains a separate product decision. **Step 3:** durable task/events, replay/approvals/recovery, external A2A, hardened transports, runtime extraction, custom sandbox tools, and channels follow named consumers. Contracted agents later use explicit separate Workspaces, governed readonly projections, and returned artifacts. The canonical plan is [`issues/391/plan.md`](issues/391/plan.md); A1/runtime details are in [`issues/805/runtime-refactor/work/A1-agent-authoring/PLAN.md`](issues/805/runtime-refactor/work/A1-agent-authoring/PLAN.md). |
origin/main:docs/DECISIONS.md:453:| **Supersedes / retains** | Supersedes the implicit assumption that one instance provider key is the payer for every hosted tenant Workspace. Retains package-layering/EU principles, Workspace-first web authorization, Decision 28's static fleet and invocation-scoped authority, and rejection of AgentHost, controllers, deployment content stores/publication journals, mutable runtime registries, and second composers. Decision 28 supersedes the old Workspace-type and exact shared-Sandbox wording. |
origin/main:docs/DECISIONS.md:473:| **Why** | Decision 28 requires a deployment-static fleet with no registry or controller, and requires that agents receive capabilities rather than policy sources. A single construction funnel is how that becomes enforceable instead of aspirational: one place validates the fleet, one place mints scope, one CI rule proves no consumer bypasses it. Addressing sessions per agent is what makes more than one agent possible in a workspace at all — the legacy single-agent wire cannot express which agent a session belongs to. |
